\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to stop ruble collapse\b0\par\par\uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced an extraordinary monetary policy meeting on Tuesday after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to 100 roubles per dollar, its lowest since March 2022.\par \par \uc2 The ruble has depreciated 30% against the dollar since the start of the year due to falling exports, rising taxes and military spending.\par \par \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced an extraordinary meeting on Tuesday on the level of interest rates, which the issuer raised in July to 8.5%, above market expectations.\par \par \uc2 The results of the meeting will be announced at 10:30 a.m. local time (04:30 a.m. ET), the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 News of the meeting reassured the market and the ruble regained ground.\par \par \uc2 During the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a level of 100 rubles per dollar and 110 per euro. By the end of the day, it advanced to 98 per dollar and 107 per euro.\par \par \uc2 The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not fallen to the level of 100 units per euro since March 2022, when it collapsed following the military offensive against Ukraine that began in February of that year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced the meeting after Kremlin adviser \uc2 Maxim Oreshkin\uc2  criticized the issuer's "loose monetary policy" in an opinion piece published by the official TASS news agency on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Oreshkin said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has all the "necessary tools" to deal with the situation and estimated that the ruble price will return to a situation of normality in the near future.\par \par \uc2 - 'Everything will go up' -\par \par \uc2 The devaluation of the ruble raises fears due to its impact on the standard of living of the general population in a context of rising inflation.\par \par \uc2 After a year and a half of sanctions by Western powers over the conflict in Ukraine, which have seen many foreign companies leave the country, Russians are beginning to feel the consequences.\par \par \uc2 "Of course I'm upset," Evgeny Kundratas, a 44-year-old human resources executive, told AFP. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more expensive and that is not convenient," he added.\par \par \uc2 Viktor Rybakov, a 61-year-old man who works in the medical sector, fears the impact on everyday life.\par \par \uc2 "Now everything will go up, from transportation to food prices," he said.\par \par \uc2 Anna Rebrova, a 33-year-old public relations manager, is more optimistic.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230814ej8e00cqv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
