\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Stocks hit one-month low; cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fails to boost rouble\b0\par\par\uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2023\par 11:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Country Garden at record low on restructuring fears\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pakistan shares jump, more firms added to key MSCI index\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Czech rate-setters see no Q3 cut - Aug. 3 minutes\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Romanian inflation falls to single digits\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pakistan leaders seek deal on caretaker PM ahead of election\par \par \uc2 By Ankika Biswas\par \par \uc2 Aug 11 (Reuters) - Emerging market stocks fell to a one-month low on Friday, dragged down by Chinese shares on concern over a rocky post-pandemic recovery and lack of concrete stimulus, while \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rouble weakened despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The MSCI EM stocks index shed 0.9% and was poised for a second weekly loss, weighed down by China's blue-chips and Hong Kong shares.\par \par \uc2 China's largest private property developer Country Garden plunged to a record low after a first-half loss forecast and a media report citing debt restructuring plans.\par \par \uc2 Ratings agency \uc2 Moody's\uc2  on Thursday downgraded the company's corporate family rating to Caa1 from B1.\par \par \uc2 Other Asian stocks were also headed for weekly losses, with Taiwan among the worst hit.\par \par \uc2 Pakistan's benchmark share index jumped over 2% after MSCI added 15 domestic-listed companies to its main Frontier Market index.\par \par \uc2 The MSCI EM \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  index slipped 0.4%, also poised for a second weekly decline, with the dollar headed for a fourth weekly gain.\par \par \uc2 U.S. consumer prices increasing moderately in July bolstered bets that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  may halt its rate-hike campaign, while the yen neared the key 145-mark, a level at which investors think the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Stable U.S. inflation should support EM rates in the medium term," analysts at \uc2 Barclays\uc2  wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 "However, the outlook for the Chinese economy puts a drag on EM \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an asset class. The expected announcement of a China stimulus package, especially focused on the real estate sector, could turn China sentiment, which remains depressed."\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, a Reuters poll showed China's new yuan loans are expected to fall sharply month-on-month in July after record lending in the first half, but could still exceed the year-earlier amount amid more economic support.\par \par \uc2 Russia's rouble headed back towards the 98-per-dollar mark and touched the 108-per-euro, but depreciated at a slower pace than much of August after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Czech's crown gained 0.4% against the euro, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its August meeting minutes noting it does not see room for policy easing in the third quarter amid persistent inflation risks.\par \par \uc2 Data showed Romanian headline inflation fell below 10% for the first time in seventeen months, but not significant enough to trigger rate cuts before next year.\par \par \uc2 On Pakistan's political front, the premier's office noted the outgoing prime minister and opposition leader will meet again on Friday to try to pick a caretaker leader to oversee a general election due by November. The rupee was down 0.3%.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, economists expect Turkish consumer prices to jump by as much as 8.5% in August, underlining Ankara's challenge amid a painful path toward more orthodox policies. (Reporting by Ankika Biswas in Bengaluru; Editing by Sharon Singleton) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-8-11T10:12:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230811ej8b0101a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
