\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Rouble weakens again after temporary pause on c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2023\par 12:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices as of 0956 GMT)\par \par \uc2 By Alexander Marrow\par \par \uc2 Aug 10 (Reuters) - The rouble weakened on Thursday, heading back towards a more than 16-month low against the dollar following a slight pause in its depreciation trend after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to try and stabilise its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia on Wednesday said it would stop conducting the finance ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases as prescribed by Russia's budget rule from Thursday, in order to reduce market volatility.\par \par \uc2 The rouble strengthened in early trade on Thursday, but by 0956 GMT, it was 0.4% weaker against the dollar at 97.57 ,\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, it had sunk to 98.0725 on Wednesday, its weakest point against the dollar since March 25, 2022, hampered by strong foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand and limited supply.\par \par \uc2 It had lost 0.9% to trade at 107.50 versus the euro and shed 0.4% against the yuan to 13.49 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move ultimately means the net supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market will increase to 2.3 billion roubles ($23.74 million) from 500 million roubles a day.\par \par \uc2 At its weakest, the rouble was around 28% weaker against the dollar year-to-date. Analysts, who had been expecting Russia's monetary authorities to act, generally said greater action would still be required to make a significant difference.\par \par \uc2 "These are not even half measures, but under-measures given the scale of the volumes," said Dmitry Polevoy, head of investment at Locko-Invest.\par \par \uc2 "The news is positive, but it will not be enough to start strengthening the rouble. We are waiting for an increase in oil revenues and a decrease in dollar and yuan demand from importers," said Alexey Antonov of Alor Broker.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil, a global benchmark for Russia's main export, was down 0.1% at $87.43 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes were higher.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was up 0.8% to 1,012.3 points. The rouble-based MOEX Russian index was 1.1% higher at 3,134.3 points.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 96.8750 roubles) (Reporting by Alexander Marrow; Editing by Alex Richardson and Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-8-10T11:11:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230810ej8a01i39\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
