\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Stocks,  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  muted ahead of US inflation data, Russia's rouble extends recovery\b0\par\par\uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2023\par 11:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russia abandons budget rule to save tanking rouble\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pakistan parliament dissolved before national election\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Egypt July headline inflation rises to record 36.5%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kenya holds rates, introduces rate corridor\par \par \uc2 By Ankika Biswas\par \par \uc2 Aug 10 (Reuters) - Most emerging market stocks and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were subdued on Thursday, as traders braced for a U.S. inflation print to gauge the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's monetary policy outlook, while the rouble extended its recovery following \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The MSCI indexes for EM stocks and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were almost unchanged, with the dollar shedding 0.3%.\par \par \uc2 Focus lies on the July inflation reading from the United States later in the day, with China's descent to deflation already denting sentiment and investors seeking concrete government stimulus.\par \par \uc2 However, China and Hong Kong shares reversed early losses to close higher, as the lifting of a pandemic-era ban on outbound group tours boosted airline and travel-related stocks.\par \par \uc2 The rouble firmed against the dollar, extending its recovery from a more than 16-month low after \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, while effectively abandoning budget rule to stabilise its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At its weakest, the rouble was around 28% weaker against the dollar year-to-date. Many analysts said greater action would still be required to make a significant difference.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Pakistan's president dissolved the parliament on Prime Minister \uc2 Shehbaz Sharif\uc2 's advice late Wednesday night, three days ahead of the parliament's five-year term, to be followed with a caretaker administration to hold new elections in 90 days.\par \par \uc2 "Starting the election process will be welcomed by investors hoping for prudent economic policy decisions by a technocratic interim caretaker administration and mindful that the \uc2 IMF\uc2  deal is a short-term term one and a notionally democratic government will have to be in place to renew it," said Hasnain Malik, emerging and frontier markets equity strategy at Tellimer.\par \par \uc2 "For civil society and political risk, the crackdown on Imran Khan and the PTI might make the election look more like a rubber-stamping process by the military elite."\par \par \uc2 The rupee was flat against the greenback, while the benchmark stock index was down 0.3%.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's forint notched strong gains, up 0.5% against the euro, with the Czech crown see-sawing after data showed headline inflation eased further into single-digit territory in July.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation is coming down more or less as expected, which should be dovish message for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing with the uncertainty about inflation falling towards the 2% target," ING's EMEA \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  & Fixed Income Strategist Frantisek Taborsky noted.\par \par \uc2 Further on the data front, Turkey's industrial production rose 1.6% month-on-month in June, while Egypt's July annual headline inflation rose to an all-time high of 36.5%, in line with expectations.\par \par \uc2 Kenya held its benchmark lending rate at 10.5%, while seeking to introduce a new rate corridor of plus or minus 250 basis points around the policy rate.\par \par \uc2 Within Latin America, traders looked ahead to key rate decisions in Peru and Mexico, after Brazil and Chile recently kicked off monetary policy easing. (Reporting by Ankika Biswas in Bengaluru; editing by Christina Fincher) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-8-10T10:02:53.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230810ej8a01aol\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
