\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Ruble sinks to 15-month lows and returns to early war\b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The ruble even skidded about 3% against the dollar this Monday, trading at 15-month lows as investors digested the hectic weekend in Russia, with the threat of a "rebellion" by the Wagner paramilitary group.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "eased" to a 1.06% drop, with each dollar worth 84.56 rubles, holding at lows from March last year - weeks after Russia's invasion of Ukraine. Since the beginning of the year, the ruble has already depreciated more than 14% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin announced Saturday night that the leader of the Wagner paramilitary group, Yevgueni Prigozhin, the protagonist of an attempted armed "rebellion" in Russia, will leave for Belarus, assuring that Russian justice will not pursue him or his fighters criminally.\par \par \uc2 Also Read \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the ruble \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  branded the group's action as rebellion, saying it was a "deadly threat" to the Russian state and treason, assuring that he would not let a "civil war" happen and that those responsible would pay for it.\par \par \uc2 At the end of the day when the Wagner group's forces advanced to about 200 kilometers from Moscow, Prigozhin announced that he had negotiated an agreement with Belarusian President \uc2 Alexander Lukashenko\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the head of the paramilitary group accused the Russian Army of attacking camps of its mercenaries, causing "a very large number of victims," accusations that expose deep tensions within Moscow's forces over the offensive in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Read Also Russia to stop selling hydrocarbons in dollars and euros Wagner Group pariahs threaten Africa Russia sees oil and gas revenues shrink more than 40 percent in March Kremlin seeks to restore "calm" after deal to stop Wagner Group rebellion\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230626ej6q00774\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
