\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russia to increase daily  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  sales in coming month\b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2023\par 13:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates, adds detail in paragraphs 6, 9-10)\par \par \uc2 By Alexander Marrow and Darya Korsunskaya\par \par \uc2 June 5 (Reuters) - \uc2 Russia's finance ministry\uc2  will increase daily foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales to the equivalent of 3.6 billion roubles ($44.3 million) a day between June 7 and July 6, it said on Monday, far exceeding analyst forecasts as it compensates for reduced fuel revenues.\par \par \uc2 After a hiatus of several months, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January, selling yuan rather than what it terms "unfriendly" Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , underscoring the growing importance of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as Moscow seeks to ensure economic stability in the face of Western sanctions.\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry said its regular \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales on the market would total 74.6 billion roubles over the coming month. Analysts surveyed by Reuters had predicted sales would total 20 billion roubles.\par \par \uc2 In the previous period, between May 10 and June 6, the ministry had planned to sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth 40.4 billion roubles to compensate for lower oil and gas revenues.\par \par \uc2 The government carries out \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cover shortfalls - or build up reserves in the event of a surplus - in earnings from Russia's vital oil and gas exports, revenues from which have shrunk this year due to Western sanctions.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold almost 450 billion roubles' worth of yuan and gold from the National Wealth Fund (\uc2 NWF\uc2 ) on the finance ministry's behalf between January and May.\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry said May's oil and gas revenues were 30.6 billion roubles below plan. It said it expected a 44-billion-rouble shortfall from federal energy revenues in June.\par \par \uc2 Reduced revenues and soaring spending pushed Russia's Jan-April budget deficit to almost $44 billion, already 17% higher than the target for all of 2023, creating fiscal pressure as Moscow continues its military offensive in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The ministry had been reducing its monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales, and analysts had been waiting for it to begin buying rather than selling. Forecasting volumes is complicated by a lack of information on oil production dynamics.\par \par \uc2 "A regime switch from selling yuan to (large-scale) \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases would be significant," \uc2 Rosbank\uc2  analysts said. The ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  help Russian banks maintain yuan liquidity, \uc2 Rosbank\uc2  said. ($1 = 81.2075 roubles) (Reporting by Darya Korsunskaya and Alexander Marrow; Editing by Toby Chopra, Sharon Singleton and Barbara Lewis) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-6-5T12:23:29.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230605ej6501825\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
