\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russian to sell 2 bln roubles of  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  daily in coming month\b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2023\par 11:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail on energy revenues, deficit, \uc2 NWF\uc2 , analyst)\par \par \uc2 May 4 (Reuters) - \uc2 Russia's finance ministry\uc2  said on Thursday it would sell 2 billion roubles' ($25 million) worth of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a day between May 10 and June 6, a decrease in the volume of daily \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the previous month.\par \par \uc2 After a hiatus of several months, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January, selling yuan rather than what it terms "unfriendly" Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , underscoring the growing importance of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Moscow's efforts to ensure economic stability amid Western sanctions.\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry said its regular \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales on the market would total 40.4 billion roubles ($513 million) over the coming month. A Reuters survey of analysts had predicted sales would total 27.5 billion roubles.\par \par \uc2 In the previous period, between April 7 and May 5, the ministry had planned to sell 74.6 billion roubles' worth of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to compensate for lower oil and gas revenues.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  halted \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year as Western nations imposed sweeping sanctions against Moscow, including the freezing of about $300 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, after it sent its armed forces into Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The government carries out \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cover shortfalls - or build up reserves in the event of a surplus - in earnings from Russia's vital oil and gas exports.\par \par \uc2 The ministry forecast the shortfall in oil and gas revenues to the budget in May at 8.1 billion roubles. In April, those revenues were 32.4 billion roubles less than expected.\par \par \uc2 Russia's federal budget balance sank to a deficit of 2.4 trillion roubles ($31 billion) in the first quarter of the year as Moscow spent heavily and energy revenues fell.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 409.1 billion roubles' worth of yuan from the National Wealth Fund (\uc2 NWF\uc2 ) on the finance ministry's behalf between January and April.\par \par \uc2 Extra commodity income from June onwards may lead to small foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases, said Dmitry Polevoy, head of investment at Locko-Invest.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 78.7000 roubles)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Darya Korsunskaya and Alexander Marrow; Editing by Kevin Liffey) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-5-4T10:33:19.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230504ej5401q46\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
