\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  rules out  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  market  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  to support ruble\b0\par\par\uc2 210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The governor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 BCR\uc2 ) ruled out on Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the ruble, which has depreciated since early March by nearly 10 percent against the dollar and by nearly 23 percent against the euro. "We know from experience that attempts to manage the exchange rate do indeed lead to sharp devaluations, to financial crises," \uc2 BCR\uc2  Governor Elvira Nabiulina told a joint session of several Duma economic committees. The head of the Bank of Russia noted that the monetary regulator is in favor of a more stable \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but is against the administrative determination of the exchange rate in order not to distort economic realities and to maintain a balance between the interests of exporters and importers. Read Also Russia sees gas and oil revenues shrink by more than 40% in March According to Nabiulina, the weakening of the ruble is associated with reduced exports and lower oil prices.\par \par \uc2  The official exchange rate for the ruble today was 82.17 rubles to the dollar and 89.72 rubles to the euro. On March 1 the ruble was equivalent to 74.89 dollars and 79.51 euros.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230412ej4c006p2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
