\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russian rouble falls as oil prices plumb new 3-month depths\b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2023\par 13:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds second bond auction)\par \par \uc2 March 15 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble weakened on lower oil prices on Wednesday, as the finance ministry held debt auctions and investors looked ahead to this week's interest rate decision by the Bank of Russia.\par \par \uc2 By 1241 GMT, the rouble was 0.9% weaker against the dollar at 75.98 and had gained 0.3% to trade at 80.39 against the euro. It had shed 0.5% against the yuan to 10.99.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude, a global benchmark for Russia's main export, was down 2% at $75.9 a barrel, its lowest mark since mid-December.\par \par \uc2 The rouble hit its strongest level against the dollar since the start of March early on Tuesday, before easing. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come under pressure from fears of a broader banking crisis following the collapse of \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are providing some support to the rouble, as \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling 5.4 billion roubles ($71.7 million) worth of Chinese yuan per day between March 7 and April 6 to compensate for lower oil and gas revenues.\par \par \uc2 Domestic attention is focused on \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which will set interest rates on Friday and has signalled it will weigh up hiking rates in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 Analysts polled by Reuters widely expect the bank to hold its key interest rate at 7.5% before possibly raising the cost of borrowing later this year.\par \par \uc2 Russia's finance ministry\uc2  sold 74.7 billion roubles in OFZ treasury bonds at auctions on Wednesday, with one still to come, after a pause in debt issuance last week.\par \par \uc2 "Investors will continue to be cautious in the debt market ahead of this Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting," said \uc2 Promsvyazbank\uc2  analysts. "With expectations that the key rate will be held, the regulator's signal will likely remain quite hawkish."\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes were lower.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was down 2% to 938.9 points. The rouble-based MOEX Russian index was 1.1% lower at 2,264.5 points. ($1 = 75.3700 roubles) (Reporting by Alexander Marrow; editing by Barbara Lewis, Tomasz Janowski and Alex Richardson) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-3-15T13:59:40.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230315ej3f01xtx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
