\par\par \b \uc2 Russian rouble steadies as oil prices pull away from 3-month lows\b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2023\par 08:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 March 15 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble stabilised ahead of three government debt auctions on Wednesday, gaining support as oil prices pulled away from over three-month lows while investors looked ahead to this week's interest rate decision by the Bank of Russia.\par \par \uc2 At 0721 GMT, the rouble was 0.1% weaker against the dollar at 75.41 and had lost 0.3% to trade at 80.90 versus the euro. It was steady against the yuan at 10.93.\par \par \uc2 The rouble hit its strongest level against the dollar since the start of March early on Tuesday, before easing. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come under pressure from fears of a spillover banking crisis following the collapse of \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are providing some support to the rouble, as \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling 5.4 billion roubles ($71.7 million) a day of Chinese yuan between March 7 and April 6 to compensate for lower oil and gas revenues.\par \par \uc2 Domestic attention is focused on \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which will set interest rates on Friday. The regulator has signalled it will weigh up hiking rates in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 Analysts polled by Reuters widely expect the bank to hold its key interest rate at 7.5% before possibly hiking the cost of borrowing later this year.\par \par \uc2 Russia's finance ministry\uc2  is set to offer OFZ treasury bonds at auction later on Wednesday after a pause in debt issuance last week.\par \par \uc2 "Investors will continue to be cautious in the debt market ahead of this Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting," said \uc2 Promsvyazbank\uc2  analysts. "With expectations that the key rate will be held, the regulator's signal will likely remain quite hawkish."\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil, a global benchmark for Russia's main export, was up 1.2% at $78.4 a barrel, pulling clear of its lowest mark since mid-December, hit in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes were mixed.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was down 0.1% to 957.2 points. The rouble-based MOEX Russian index was 0.1% higher at 2,291.4 points. ($1 = 75.3700 roubles) (Reporting by Alexander Marrow; editing by Barbara Lewis) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-3-15T08:32:13.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230315ej3f012i5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
