\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-With a sale of Chinese yuan,  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  kicks off 2023  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2023\par 12:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to resume \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yuan amid lower oil and gas revenue\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Use of yuan underscores greater role of China\par \par \uc2 (Recasts headline and lead, adds quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Guy Faulconbridge and Darya Korsunskaya\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Jan 11 (Reuters) -\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would resume foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the sale of yuan from Friday, underscoring the growing importance of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Moscow's efforts to ensure economic stability amid Western sanctions.\par \par \uc2 After the West imposed the most severe sanctions in modern history over the war in Ukraine, Russia's economy has shown remarkable resilience but the world's biggest producer of natural resources is now turning increasingly towards China.\par \par \uc2 Chinese students have flocked to Russian universities, Mandarin graces signs in Moscow tourist spots alongside English and Russian, and President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  has touted a "no limits" partnership with President \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Russia's finance ministry\uc2 , which along with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  led Moscow's economic response to the sanctions, said it would sell 54.5 billion roubles ($798 million) in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Jan. 13 amid lower oil and gas revenues.\par \par \uc2 "In order to increase the stability and predictability of domestic economic conditions, as well as to reduce the impact of volatile energy market conditions on the Russian economy and public finances, the Finance Ministry will resume \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the purchase/sale of liquid assets," the ministry said.\par \par \uc2 Russia's 2023 budget is based on a Urals blend price of around $70.1 a barrel, though Russia's main blend is currently trading at below $50 a barrel. Russian nominal GDP is likely to be $2.14 trillion this year, the highest level since 2013, according to the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Russia, where the U.S. dollar was king for years following the collapse of the Soviet Union in 1991, China's yuan, or renminbi, has become a major player in Moscow since the imposition of Western sanctions.\par \par \uc2 Its share of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market reached 48% in November, MOEX Group said last month, up from less than 1% at the start of 2022.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would carry out \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions on the yuan market of the Moscow Exchange - the yuan-rouble for settlement tomorrow (CNYRUB_TOM).\par \par \uc2 "To minimize the impact of these \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the dynamics of the exchange rate, the Bank of Russia will buy (sell) foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market evenly during each trading day of the month," the bank said.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 68.6875 roubles) (Reporting by Reuters Writing by Guy Faulconbridge Editing by Gareth Jones) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-1-11T12:12:56.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230111ej1b01620\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
