\par\par \b \uc2 Russian rouble hits near 2-week high vs dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2022\par 10:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * This content was produced in Russia where the law restricts coverage of Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, July 18 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble strengthened to a near two-week high against the dollar on Monday, heading towards the 56 mark, boosted by a favourable tax payment period and capital controls as market players looked ahead to a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate decision this week.\par \par \uc2 The rouble is set to see extra support towards the end this month as export-focused companies usually step up conversion of their \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenues to meet local liabilities. Tax payments began last week and the bulk are due in the last week of July.\par \par \uc2 At 0752 GMT, the rouble was 1.2% stronger against the dollar at 56.48, earlier touching 56.3425, its strongest mark since July 5.\par \par \uc2 It had gained 1.5% to trade at 57.12 versus the euro , earlier hitting a two-week high of 56.97.\par \par \uc2 "There is still potential for the rouble to strengthen," said \uc2 Promsvyazbank\uc2  in a note, suggesting the rouble could move to the lower end of the 56-58 range against the greenback, supported by approaching tax and dividend payments.\par \par \uc2 The rouble is the world's best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://emea1.apps.cp.thomsonreuters.com/Apps/NewsServices/mediaProxy?apiKey=6d416f26-7b24-4f31-beb6-1b5aa0f3fafb&url=http%3A%2F%2Ffingfx.thomsonreuters.com%2Fgfx%2Frngs%2FGLOBAL-CURRENCIES-PERFORMANCE%2F0100301V041%2Findex.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  so far this year, boosted by measures - including restrictions on Russian households withdrawing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  savings - taken to shield Russia's financial system from Western sanctions imposed after Moscow sent troops into Ukraine on Feb. 24.\par \par \uc2 The rouble's strength has concerned officials as it dents Russia's income from exporting commodities and other goods priced in dollars and euros. Finance Minister \uc2 Anton Siluanov\uc2  has said \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  could turn to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation can be restrained either by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  or by increasing import opportunities," German Gref, CEO of dominant lender \uc2 Sberbank\uc2 , was quoted as saying by news agencies on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 The rouble may see weaker upside pressure from interest rates at home this week as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to cut its key rate from 9.5% at the July 22 board meeting after Russia posted a drop in consumer prices in June.\par \par \uc2 Veles Capital analysts said an interest rate cut on Friday was likely.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes were mixed.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was up 0.9% to 1,172.3 points, at its highest since July 5. The rouble-based MOEX Russian index was 0.2% lower at 2,105.4 points. (Reporting by Reuters) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-18T09:08:33.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220718ei7i00z9i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
