\par\par \b \uc2 Russians rush to buy Chinese yuan, Otkritie bank says\b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2022\par 15:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 July 7 (Reuters) - Russians have rushed to buy Chinese yuan to diversify their holdings away from U.S. dollars and euros, the state bank Otkritie said, as the finance ministry aims to re-start \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  using 'friendly' nations' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Demand for the yuan has increased eightfold since May 20 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted the restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 -buying that it introduced to limit the impact of western sanctions on the financial sector, Otkritie, under sanctions itself, said in a note.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, purchases of the British pound and Swiss francs by Russians have increased 2.5 times, while other once popular \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the U.S. dollar and the euro, were less in demand, Otkritie added.\par \par \uc2 "The Chinese yuan has shown stability and relatively low volatility over the past years, and it can become the main tool for diversifying \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  savings," Aliya Zubkova, deputy head of the financial markets department at Otkritie, told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Rouble-yuan trading volumes hit a record high of 44.3 billion roubles ($703 million) this week, the \uc2 Moscow Exchange\uc2  said, as the finance ministry seeks to re-start \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying using what Russia terms 'friendly' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the rouble's growth.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Moscow Exchange\uc2  launched rouble-yuan trading in 2013 and in April, its daily trading volumes reached 25 billion roubles.\par \par \uc2 Authorities in \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  via market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early 2022, under a budget rule designed to shield the rouble from external shocks and ease pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that was falling sharply.\par \par \uc2 It has recovered strongly, climbing to seven-year highs just over a week ago.\par \par \uc2 The rouble remains the world's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year even though it has shed about 20% against the dollar since last month's peaks as officials voiced concerns about its strength, which dents Russia's income from exporting commodities and other goods priced in dollars and euros.\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry has yet to announce how it plans to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying.\par \par \uc2 Economists say the comfortable level for the rouble would be around 70-80 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 63.0500 roubles) (Reporting by Reuters; editing by Barbara Lewis) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-7T14:03:48.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220707ei7702ahh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
