\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Strong dollar dents Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  after Powell comments\b0\par\par\uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 2022\par 17:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * S&P cuts China 2022 GDP forecast, says EM growth to slow \par     * Brazil's real recovers from more than four-month lows\par     * Other \f28 \uc2 \f2 Latam\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slip as dollar gains strength\par     * Russia looks to curb rouble rally\par \par     By Susan Mathew\par     June 29 (Reuters) - Most Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gave up\par early gains on Wednesday as the dollar strengthened following\par some hawkish comments by \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  policymakers,\par while Russia's rouble pared gains as the finance ministry looked\par to curb the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's surge. \par     Mexico's peso was flat, while some other regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell between 0.1% and 0.7%. \par     Brazil's real outperformed, up 0.7%, recovering from\par over four-month lows hit last session. Brazil plans to simplify\par procedures for issuing private bonds to stimulate fundraising\par through capital markets, an economy ministry official told\par Reuters.\par     Fed chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jerome Powell\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Wednesday stuck to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's hawkish stance citing surging inflation as a bigger risk.\par This followed hawkish comments from Fed policymakers pushing for\par big and faster interest rate hikes, denting risk appetite and\par lifting the dollar.\par     "Emerging markets and commodities could stay under pressure\par if the (dollar) stays bouncy," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 AJ Bell\f28 \uc2 \f2  Investment Director\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russ Mould\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     "Many emerging nations borrow in dollars, and weakness in\par their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the American one makes it more\par expensive to pay the coupons and eventually repay the original\par loans."\par     Fears that aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tightening will push\par economies into recession have gripped markets this year. MSCI's\par index of EM shares is on course for its biggest\par quarterly drop since a coronavirus driven rout in the first\par quarter of 2020, and its worst first half since at least 2008.  \par     EM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are on track for their weakest\par first half performance since 2020. \par     Looking ahead, emerging market economies will slow in the\par second half of this year amid high inflation, ratings agency S&P\par said, cutting GDP growth prediction for China to 3.3%, from 4.2%\par in May.\par     Russia's rouble pared some gains after\par it hit 50 to the dollar as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister flagged\par possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ease upward pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par It may start buying the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of "friendly" countries and\par use those holdings to try to influence the exchange rate of the\par dollar and euro.\par     The rouble has soared to seven-year highs, boosted by\par capital controls that include curbs on Russians withdrawing\par foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  savings, thereby eating into Russia's export\par income by denting the value of dollar and euro proceeds from\par sales abroad of commodities and other goods.\par     South Africa's rand extended losses to a two-week low\par as state power utility \f28 \uc2 \f2 Eskom\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it would resume "Stage 6"\par power cuts.\par     Tracking a choppy session on Wall Street, most \f28 \uc2 \f2 Latam\f28 \uc2 \f2  bourses\par were lower, with Colombia's main index down 1.0%.\par Brazil's Bovespa index fell 0.4% with losses capped by a\par 0.9% rise in oil firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2  as crude prices\par firmed. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1433 GMT:\par    Stock indexes            Latest    Daily %\par                                       change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets       1013.65    -1.59\par                                       \par  MSCI LatAm                  2081.22    -0.72\par                                       \par  Brazil Bovespa            100173.28    -0.42\par                                       \par  Mexico IPC                 48108.54    -0.67\par                                       \par  Chile IPSA                  4997.38    -0.17\par                                       \par  Argentina MerVal           88147.10   -0.054\par                                       \par  Colombia COLCAP             1367.48    -0.99\par                                       \par                                              \par        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2            Latest    Daily %\par                                       change\par  Brazil real                  5.2306     0.68\par                                       \par  Mexico peso                 20.1280    -0.03\par                                       \par  Chile peso                    918.1    -0.82\par                                       \par  Colombia peso                4117.6    -0.75\par  Argentina peso             125.0400    -