\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russia may buy 'friendly' countries'  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  to weaken rouble -Siluanov\b0\par\par\uc2 456 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 2022\par 14:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * This content was produced in Russia where the law restricts coverage of Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine (Adds detail, officials' comments)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, June 29 (Reuters) - Russia may start buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of "friendly" countries and use those holdings to try to influence the exchange rate of the dollar and euro, as a means of countering sharp gains in the rouble, its finance minister said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has soared to seven-year highs, boosted by capital controls that include curbs on Russians withdrawing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  savings, thereby eating into Russia's export income by denting the value of dollar and euro proceeds from sales abroad of commodities and other goods.\par \par \uc2 Authorities in \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  via market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early 2022, under a budget rule designed to shield it from external shocks, to ease pressure on the rouble at a time when it was falling sharply.\par \par \uc2 Those declines were triggered by fears of tough Western sanctions in the run-up to what Moscow calls the "special military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in Ukraine that began on Feb. 24.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Anton Siluanov\uc2  said that, under a "modified" budget rule, his ministry was ready to step in and accumulate other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its reserves.\par \par \uc2 "Through the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of friendly countries, through cross-rates with the dollar and the euro it will be possible to regulate the cost of the euro and the dollar to the rouble," he told a conference organised by a Russian business lobby group.\par \par \uc2 "...We will discuss this with the economic bloc in the government. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has agreed."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Elvira Nabiullina\uc2 , who was speaking at the same conference, said the bank - which maintains a floating rouble policy - was ready to take part in the trade to increase liquidity in other nations' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Exporters were ready to switch to other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  while importers preferred dollars and euros, she said.\par \par \uc2 Siluanov gave no other details of how the scheme might work, though the rouble pared gains after his and Nabiullina's comments, heading away from levels around 50 against the dollar that it had neared for the first time since May 2015.\par \par \uc2 With Russia looking for ways to soften the sanctions blow on its financial sector, Siluanov said his ministry would also suggest allowing export-focused companies to receive proceeds from non-residents in cash.\par \par \uc2 The Moscow \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange this week started trading the South African rand and the Armenian dram, and is preparing to launch trading in the Uzbek sum and the United Arab Emirates dirham. It has been trading the Chinese yuan for years.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Reuters; editing by John Stonestreet) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-6-29T13:28:03.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220629ei6t01ua6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
