\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The ruble strengthens today against the dollar to values not seen since 2015\b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 With information from EFE\par \par \uc2 The ruble continues to strengthen against the dollar and the euro, and today was trading at its strongest value since June and May 2015, respectively, on the Moscow Stock Exchange.\par \par \uc2 At 11:10 a.m. Peruvian time (15:10 GMT) the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 53.91 rubles to the dollar unit, the first price below 54 rubles since June 24, 2015, according to business daily RBK.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also being bought at 56.65 rubles per euro, a value not seen since May 2015. Thus, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russia\uc2  has set the official exchange rate for tomorrow at 54.70 rubles per dollar and 57.45 rubles per euro.\par \par \uc2 Thus, the ruble has more than doubled in almost four months since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plummeted at the start of the Russian military campaign in Ukraine last February 24.\par \par \uc2 The ruble then fell to levels not seen since 1994 and 1994 against the dollar and the euro, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls allowed the bleeding to be reversed.\par \par \uc2 The strengthening of the ruble comes against the backdrop of the approaching tax payment period and high prices on commodity markets, according to Otrkitie Investments analyst Andrei Kochetkov.\par \par \uc2 The current demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not cover the oversupply in the market by exporters, which puts pressure on the dollar and the euro, he said. The day before, the number two in the Russian government, \uc2 Andrei Belousov\uc2 , told the Interfax agency that the authorities are considering returning the ruble to its "optimal quotation."\par \par \uc2 "As for the ruble's optimal rate there is a more or less consensus opinion that it is in the range of 70-80 rubles to the dollar," the Russian deputy prime minister said. Asked about the time frame in which the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should reach its optimal rate, Belousov replied, "As soon as possible."\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220622ei6m00anh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
