\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war live: Russian shelling in Donbas intensifies and Zelenski speaks of "hell".\b0\par\par\uc2 6,095 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 LIVENews inDevelopmentShelling by Russian troops against fifty villages in the Donbas\par \par \uc2 caused about twenty deaths, in a context which the Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymir Zelenski\uc2 , describes as "hell".Up to 54 localities in the Donetsk and Lugansk regions\par \par \uc2 were hit hard by Russian artillery in the last 24 hours, with the death of twenty civilians, the governmental Ukrainian United Forces Grouping reported today.20.05.2022\par \par \uc2 08:07\par \par \uc2 Russia announces reconstruction plan for Ukrainian regions under its control Russia announced Friday that it has a reconstruction plan for the territories of Ukraine\par \par \uc2 that were affected by the military actions that are under the control of Russian troops."We already have the schedule of reconstruction works. We have created a special cabinet, in which all interested agencies participate," said Russian Deputy Prime Minister Marat Jusnulin, quoted by the Interfax agency, during a working visit to Kazan, the capital of the Russian republic of Tatarstan.\par \par \uc2 He added that specialists are already in those Ukrainian territories to assess the reconstruction work required.\par \par \uc2 20.05.2022\par \par \uc2 07:47\par \par \uc2 Russian shelling in the Donbas intensifies and Zelensky speaks of "hell "Photo of an art installation with a wooden map of Ukraine with depictions of the war in the square in Lviv (Ukraine). Photo EFE/ Esteban BibaThe\par \par \uc2 bombardments of Russian troops against fifty towns in the Donbas caused about twenty deaths\par \par \uc2 , in a context that the Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymir Zelenski\uc2 , describes as "hell".Up to 54 localities in the Donetsk and Lugansk regions\par \par \uc2 were heavily hit by Russian artillery in the last 24 hours, with the death of twenty civilians, the governmental Ukrainian United Forces Group reported today."According to \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  information, about twenty civilians were killed under enemy fire and at least fifty people were wounded," the organization specifies in a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post reported by Ukrinform agency\par \par \uc2 .20.05.2022\par \par \uc2 07:21\par \par \uc2 More than 1,900 Ukrainian servicemen from Azovstal surrendered to Russian forcesADonetsk People's Republic militia APC stands not far from the besieged Azovstal steel plant in Mariupol. AP Photo.\par \par \uc2 More than 1,900 fighters blockaded at the Azovstal steel plant in the southern Ukrainian city of Mariupol have surrendered prisoners to Russian forces\par \par \uc2 since Monday, Russian Defense Minister \uc2 Sergei Shoigu\uc2  said today, raising the previously known official figures to just over 1,700."The nationalists blockaded at the plant have begun to surrender. So far 1,908 people have laid down their arms," Shoigu said at a Defense Ministry meeting, Sputnik and AFP news agencies reported.\par \par \uc2 20.05.2022\par \par \uc2 05:09\par \par \uc2 European companies should pay for Russian natural gas ineurosEuropean companies should pay for Russian natural gas exclusively in euros, said \uc2 Frans Timmermans\uc2 , vice-president of the \uc2 European Commission\par \par \uc2 .Commenting on media reports that several major European gas companies have opened accounts with \uc2 Gazprombank\uc2  (Russia), through which payments made in euros are converted into Russian rubles, he told Estonian broadcaster ERR on Friday that "this is not normal."\par \par \uc2 "The agreements are very clear, the agreements mention euros and dollars. This is normal. But not rubles. With this trick that Putin is trying to use, he is trying to keep his \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  afloat with foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is not allowed by sanctions," said the EC vice-president. .\par \par \uc2 20.05.2022\par \par \uc2 04:50\par \par \uc2 Russian attacks on Severodonetsk leave 12 deadIna message posted on the Telegram app on Friday, \uc2 Serhiy Haidai\uc2 , governor of Luhansk oblast, noted that the offensive caused 12 deaths in Severodonetsk and destroyed more than 60 homes in the region\par \par \uc2 ."The attack on Severodonetsk was unsuccessful. The Russians suffered personal casualties and withdrew," he added.\par \par \uc2 20.05.2022\par \par \uc2 04:32\par \par \uc2 At least 232 Ukrainian children died since the beginning of the warAtleast 232 Ukrainian children died since the beginning of Russia's invasion, the Prosecutor General's Office reported. However, the real figure is estimated to be much higher, since child casualties in the areas under the control of enemy troops are not taken into consideration.\par \par \uc2 20.05.2022\par \par \uc2 03:54\par \par \uc2 Belarus bans "1984\u8243\'20\'33 by George Orwell"All editions of 1984 by G. Orwell will be withdrawn from the market. The report on the implementation will be submitted no later than May 19," reads the order of \uc2 Alexander Lukashenko\uc2 's government, opposition newspaper Nasha Niva reported.?\par \par \uc2 20.05.2022\par \par \uc2 03:30\par \par \uc2 Ukraine reported Russian casualties since the beginning of the war20.05.2022\par \par \uc2 02:54\par \par \uc2 Paris allocated 1.1 million euros to Ukraine for the restoration of Kiev and ChernihivParisallocated 1.1 million euros to Ukraine for the restoration of the Kiev and Chernihiv regions, the press service of the Embassy of Ukraine in France reported .\par \par \uc2 "The French Paris region has decided to allocate 1.1 million euros for projects to support Ukraine and develop cooperation with the Kiev and Chernihiv regions," they specified in the report.\par \par \uc2 20.05.2022\par \par \uc2 02:13\par \par \uc2 Self-proclaimed governor of Kherson assured that that city will be annexed to RussiaAta first meeting with occupying pro-Russian collaborators in Kherson, Russian-appointed governor Volodymyr Saldo said that that city "will soon become a part" of the Russian Federation\par \par \uc2 ."We see the Russian Federation as our own country," he said, adding that the new budget of the Kherson region was approved in Russian rubles\par \par \uc2 .20.05.2022\par \par \uc2 01:07\par \par \uc2 Argentine \uc2 Rafael Grossi\uc2 , head of the \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2 , insists on visiting the Ukrainian Zaporizhzhia plantThedirector general of the \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2  (\uc2 IAEA\uc2 ), \uc2 Rafael Grossi\uc2 , insisted Friday from Tokyo on his desire to visit in the near future the Ukrainian nuclear power plant in Zaporizhzhia, under Russian military control\par \par \uc2 .Grossi referred to the trip during a courtesy visit to Japanese Prime Minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 , as part of a stay in the Asian country together with the agency's mission monitoring the situation at the accident-prone Fukushima plant and the plan to dump contaminated and processed water from the facility into the Pacific.\par \par \uc2 "It is extremely important to ensure the safety of nuclear facilities," Grossi reiterated today regarding his desire to travel soon to Zaporizhzhia, which currently remains under Russian control in the current context of the Russian-Ukrainian war.\par \par \uc2 20.05.2022\par \par \uc2 00:30\par \par \uc2 Russia blocks evacuation of more than 1,000 cars to ZaporizhzhiaTheadministration of \uc2 Volodomir Zelensky\uc2  warned that a Russian checkpoint in the town of Vasylivka delayed more than 1,000 cars with Ukrainians who are trying to escape from the areas of increased war action and find shelter in Zaporizhzhia\par \par \uc2 .19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 23:55\par \par \uc2 Zelensky anticipated that the final stage of the war will be "the bloodiest "During a speech before Ukrainian university students, President Zelensky said that he cannot yet ask Ukrainians to return home from abroad for fear that the final stage of the war will be "the most difficult, the bloodiest."\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 23:22\par \par \uc2 Ukraine revealed that the United States plans to destroy Russian ships blockading the Black SeaAntonHerashchenko, adviser to the Ukrainian government, revealed via his official twitter account that the United States plans to destroy Russian ships blockading the Black Sea.\par \par \uc2 "The United States prepares a plan for the destruction of the Black Sea Fleet. The effective work of the Ukrainians on warships convinced them to prepare a plan to unblock Ukrainian ports. Deliveries of powerful anti-ship weapons (harpoon and naval strike missiles with a range of 250-300 km) are being discussed," he wrote.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 22:50\par \par \uc2 Belarus bought missile systems from RussiaBelarusbought Iskander and S-400 missile systems from Russia, Belarusian dictator \uc2 Alexander Lukashenko\uc2  told state media Belta.Belarus also began building its own missile system similar to the Iskander, which could be complete by the end of the year with Russian support\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 22:18\par \par \uc2 New evidence shows how Russian soldiers executed Ukrainians in Bucha It is the last time the men would be seen alive: in two videos, Russian paratroopers lead them at gunpoint down a street in Bucha, a suburb of Kiev. Some of the Ukrainian captives are hunched over, holding the belts of those in front of them. Others have their hands on their heads. "Walk to the right, bitch," one of the soldiers orders them.The videos, filmed on March 4 by a security camera and a witness at a nearby house and obtained by \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 , are the clearest evidence yet that the men were in the custody of Russian troops minutes before they were executed. Read more.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 22:10\par \par \uc2 'Five Eyes' alliance prosecutors back Ukraine war crimesinvestigationsAttorneys general of the member countries of the "Five Eyes" alliance expressed their support for Ukraine's intention to prosecute war crimes that occurred in the midst of the Russian invasion, coinciding with the first trial of a foreign soldier\par \par \uc2 .The attorneys general of the United Kingdom, the United States, Australia, Canada and New Zealand said they fully support their Ukrainian counterpart, Iryna Venediktova\par \par \uc2 's pursuit of those responsible for war crimes committed since Russia launched its invasion of the territory on February 24.Ukrainian authorities claim to have opened hundreds of files on crimes allegedly committed by Russian forces.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 21:53\par \par \uc2 Volodimir Zelensky\uc2 : "We will deliver criminals to justice "In his usual video on the Telegram channel, the Ukrainian president assured that "the first trial against a Russian war criminal has already begun."\par \par \uc2 "And it will conclude with the full restoration of justice at the level of the international court. I am sure of it. We will find and deliver to justice all those who gave and executed criminal orders," Zelensky stated, in a video-message.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 21:19\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of troops surrendering in Mariupol are prisoners of war warnedThefate of hundreds of Ukrainian fighters who surrendered after resisting attacks on the Azovstal\par \par \uc2 steel plant was uncertain, amid international fears that the Russians will retaliate against the prisoners.The \uc2 International Committee of the Red Cross\uc2  collected personal information on hundreds of the soldiers (name, date of birth, next of kin) and registered them as prisoners of war, as part of its role to ensure they receive humane treatment under the Geneva Conventions.\par \par \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2  said in a tweet that the Ukrainian soldiers are now prisoners of war and, as such, "must not be subjected to any form of torture or ill-treatment."\par \par \uc2 More than 1,700 of soldiers at the Mariupol steel plant surrendered since Monday, Russian authorities reported.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 20:56\par \par \uc2 The story of the Argentine cartoonist behind the comic about Volodimir ZelenskiPabloMartitena, the Argentine cartoonist who illustrated the comic about \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2  - Photo Twitter @PabloMartinenaPablo\par \par \uc2 Martinena is from Catamarca, lives in the provincial capital and has been drawing "forever". In the last hours his name gained transcendence for being the illustrator behind a comic that has as its protagonist \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\par \par \uc2 , the Ukrainian president who resists the Russian invasion. "I've been with illustration all my life," Martinena explained in an interview with LN+.\par \par \uc2 However, the most important professional leap came around the year 2000, when he began to show his creations in different publishing houses.\par \par \uc2 Read more.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 20:20\par \par \uc2 McDonald\uc2 's found a buyer for its Russian locations and will rebrand the restaurantsLineof people looking to eat almost for the last time at \uc2 McDonald\uc2 's in Moscow. Photo EFE.\par \par \uc2 After the war in Ukraine left the country, Alexander Govor\par \par \uc2 , which currently manages 25 McDonald's restaurants in Siberia, will take over the company's restaurants and staff, and will operate them under a new brand, as reported by the fast food giant and compiled by the BBC.They reportedly did not disclose the sale price, but warned investors that the exit will involve more than $1 billion. \uc2 McDonald\uc2 's operated in Russia for more than 30 years.\par \par \uc2 The opening of its first restaurant in Moscow in 1990 came to symbolize the thawing of Cold War tensions.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 19:44\par \par \uc2 Oil cut the streak of fallsTheprice of a barrel of oil rose today in New York cutting two days of declines, as China began to open confinements and despite there are still fears of a downturn in economic activity in the Asian giant\par \par \uc2 .The barrel of the WTI variety rose 1.9% and closed at 111.60 dollars, while Brent crude gained 2% and settled at 111.20 dollars, according to figures provided by the \uc2 New York Mercantile Exchange\uc2  (NYMEX).\par \par \uc2 However, the market remains concerned that high fuel prices could affect economic growth.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 18:44\par \par \uc2 Maria Laura AvignoloPurge\par \par \uc2 in the Russian military, doubts grow over the whereabouts of two generals Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  during the Victory Day parade on May 9 last in Moscow. Photo: APWhere\par \par \uc2 are they? Two senior officers of the Russian military forces did not appear at the May 9 military parade in Moscow and are neither on the list of officers killed in the war nor on the list of missing. All believe they have fallen in the "purge" that President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  has unleashed since he launched his so far ill-fated invasion of Ukraine. A war he is personally leading. Read more.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 17:43\par \par \uc2 An Argentine cartoonist launched Zelenski's comic book It is Pablo Martinena, who unveiled his new work through his Twitter account\par \par \uc2 .The comic is called "Political Powe: \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2 " and, according to his publication, it is a biographical work of the Ukrainian president and it was edited by TidalWave Comics, an American company.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 17:38\par \par \uc2 Ukraine charged against foreign companies that did not leave Russia Through theTwitter account of the Ministry of Defense, the government of \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2  charged against the firms that decided not to close their businesses in Russia and accused them of privileging "money over people's lives"\par \par \uc2 ."There can be only one explanation why some foreign companies have not yet left Russia: money is more important to people's lives. New warlords," the publication says.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 17:33\par \par \uc2 New reports of rape by Russian soldiers Ombudsman in Ukraine denounced that this Thursday "in just one hour", 10 reports of rape "by occupiers", including 8 children, were received from newly liberated villages in the Kharkiv\par \par \uc2 region.Yesterday - 56 reports, the report adds.\par \par \uc2 In addition, notes the publication on Twitter of the \uc2 Ukrainian Defense Ministry\uc2 , that among the children, there were two 10-year-olds and another 1, who died from his wounds.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 17:21\par \par \uc2 The confessions of a former mercenary of the mysterious Wagner groupMaratGabidullin, a former mercenary of the Wagner Group, poses during an interview with Reuters in Neuilly-sur-Seine, near Paris, France May 9, 2022. REUTERS/Christian HartmannMarat\par \par \uc2 Gabidullin, a former Wagner Group fighter, publishes "Moi, Marat, ex-commandant de l'arm\u233\'00\'E9e Wagner" (I, Marat, former commander of the Wagner army, edited in France by Michel Lafon). Recruited by the Wagner military company in 2015, he slammed the door, disgusted, in 2019, and decided to tell his story which will be published in 2022 in Russia. Read more.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 17:19\par \par \uc2 "The price of food is our number one problem" David Beasley, head of the \uc2 World Food Program\uc2  - Photo EFE\par \par \uc2 "We are truly in an unprecedented crisis. The price of food is our number one problem right now," said David Beasley, head of the \uc2 World Food Program\uc2 , at a meeting of the \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2 , chaired by U.S. Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 17:15\par \par \uc2 Cross accusations between Washington and Moscow over food crisisTheUnited Statesand Russia blamed each other Thursday at the \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  for the worsening of food insecurity in the world and Washington called on Moscow to allow Ukrainian grain exports\par \par \uc2 Blockaded in the Black Sea ports."Stop blockading Black Sea ports! Allow the free movement of ships, trains and trucks carrying food out of Ukraine," said the head of U.S. diplomacy, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , at a Security Council meeting convened by the United States.\par \par \uc2 Russian Ambassador to the UN Vassily Nebenzia flatly refuted Western accusations that consist in "blaming Russia for all the world's problems."\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 17:10\par \par \uc2 For Kiev, "\uc2 NATO\uc2  did nothing during the war". Ukrainian Foreign Minister \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2  believes that \uc2 NATO\uc2  as an institution did nothing to help Ukraine over the past three months.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 European Union\uc2  proved that it is an organization capable of acting as a united front and making powerful, important and difficult decisions in comparison with \uc2 NATO\uc2 ," he said and reports Ukrinform agency.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 17:05\par \par \uc2 German Chancellor blamed Russia for the food crisis, "especially in the Southern Hemisphere." \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2 , German chancellor, blamed Moscow for the food crisis\par \par \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2 , warned Thursday of the danger of a "serious food crisis, especially in the Southern Hemisphere" due to the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 "To be clear: Russia is solely responsible for this," Scholz added, during a press conference in The Hague with Dutch Prime Minister \uc2 Mark Rutte\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The German chancellor emphasized that Russia is currently blocking Ukraine's grain export routes.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 16:01\par \par \uc2 Zelenski: Russia will always be a threat Zelenski spoke about the Russian "threat". Photo: Reuters/Valentyn Ogirenko/File image.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2  said his country may gain independence but Russia will always be there and could always be a threat.\par \par \uc2 "We need to understand that Russia will always be there. And, perhaps, it will always be a threat," Zelensky said in his speech to students and rectors of Ukrainian higher education institutions.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 15:45\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian paramedic's camera captured by Russians reveals horrors in MariupolA lauded Ukrainian paramedic recorded her stay in Mariupol on a small memory card, brought out into the world in a tampon. Now, she is a prisoner of the Russians and Mariupol is falling.\par \par \uc2 Yuliia Paievska used her body camera to record 256 gigabytes of video of her team's frantic efforts to save lives. She gave the harrowing footage to an Associated Press team as they left in a rare humanitarian caravan. Read more\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 14:47\par \par \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  approves $40 billion in aid for UkraineThe U.S. Senate on Thursday approved with a large majority a $40 billion package of military and humanitarian aid for Ukraine to deal with the war unleashed by Russia's invasion of its territory.\par \par \uc2 The measure, which was endorsed with the vote in favor of 86 senators against 11 against and had already been previously approved by the House of Representatives, will soon be signed by the President of the United States, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , for its entry into force.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 14:28\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian negotiator says no ceasefire without Russian troops withdrawalUkrainian presidential adviser Mikhailo Podolyak on Thursday rejected the possibility of agreeing a ceasefire with Russia that does not provide for the withdrawal of Russian troops from Ukrainian territory\par \par \uc2 "Do not offer us a ceasefire, it is impossible without the full withdrawal of Russian troops. Ukrainian society is not interested in a new 'Minsk' and the return of war in a few years," Podolyak tweeted in reference to the agreement named after the Belarusian capital and negotiated after the Russian annexation of Crimea.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 14:19\par \par \uc2 Russia seeks to re-establish "historical borders".The Russian government was "absolutely convinced" of the "liberation" of the Donbas and demilitarization of the surrounding territories in eastern Ukraine after the surrender of almost all defenders of the Azovstal steelworks.\par \par \uc2 "First of all, complete liberation of the historical territories awaits the Donbas. I am absolutely convinced that the Russian army and the Donetsk and Lugansk people's militias will restore the historical borders," said \uc2 Sergey Kiriyenko\uc2 , deputy head of the presidential administration, stressing that Russia aims to "demilitarize the surrounding territories so that they will stop flying missiles and shells over the territory of the Donbas."\par \par \uc2 The official pointed out that Russia "does not fight only with Ukraine (...) against us fights a unified West, just that on the territory of Ukraine and with Ukrainian hands. It is a dramatic situation, but it is so."\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 13:57\par \par \uc2 Maria Laura Avignolo\par \par \uc2 Food, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's new weapon and the risk of global hungerIn Valery Zhivaga's potato farm everything shook and the old tractor flew into the air. A Russian anti-tank mine had exploded under its front wheel. When explosives experts arrived, they discovered five other mines scattered in the field.\par \par \uc2 This is Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's strategy to generate widespread famine in the world. He has already succeeded in Sri Lanka, where food shortages and rising prices are causing total chaos. Read more\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 13:45\par \par \uc2 Russian and US Chiefs of General Staff discuss situation in UkraineChief of the General Staff of the Russian Armed Forces \uc2 Valery Gerasimov\uc2  on Thursday discussed the situation in Ukraine with his US counterpart \uc2 Mark Milley\uc2 , the \uc2 Russian Defense Ministry\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 In the phone call, which came at Milley's initiative, the two "addressed issues of mutual interest, including the situation in Ukraine," where \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly three months ago, the military entity said in a terse statement.\par \par \uc2 The conversation took place only seven days after the one between U.S. Defense Secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  and his Russian counterpart, \uc2 Sergey Shoigu\uc2 , to ask for a cease-fire in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 13:33\par \par \uc2 Ukraine expects Russia to keep its word on Azovstal prisonersRussia reported that 1,730 Ukrainian soldiers have already surrendered in Azovstal. Photo: EFE/video capture.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian army confirmed that the evacuation of soldiers fighting at the Azovstal steel mill in Mariupol continues, and said it expects Russia to keep its word to respect their lives and not subject them to torture and ill-treatment.\par \par \uc2 "Measures to evacuate Ukrainian soldiers from Mariupol are continuing," said Brigadier General Oleksii Gromov, head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  department of the Ukrainian General Staff, without giving details on the number of servicemen, which Russia says totals 1,730 fighters.\par \par \uc2 "We know that our enemy is insidious, but we believe that the given word will be kept," Gromov added, alluding to the agreement reached to evacuate the soldiers from Azovstal, which provides for them to be exchanged for Russian prisoners held by Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 13:17\par \par \uc2 Julio Alga\u241\'00\'F1araz\par \par \uc2 Arms shipment to Ukraine unleashes political storm in Italy.Recent polls are showing that misgivings are growing in public opinion in Italy over the danger that the government's delivery of armaments to Ukraine will produce retaliation from Russia.\par \par \uc2 The issue is producing strong clashes between Prime Minister \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  and some of the political forces that support him, so much so that there is even talk of the risk of "derailing" the vast alliance that brought Draghi to power in February 2021. Read more\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 13:01\par \par \uc2 Biden: Finland and Sweden meet all requirements for \uc2 NATO\uc2  membershipU.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on Thursday expressed his "resounding support" for Finland and Sweden's applications to join \uc2 NATO\uc2 , assuring that these countries "meet all the requirements to join" the alliance.\par \par \uc2 Biden also announced that this Thursday he will begin the process for the \uc2 U.S. Congress\uc2  to ratify the entry applications of these Nordic countries, during a press conference at the White House together with his Finnish counterpart, \uc2 Sauli Niinist\u246\'00\'F6\uc2 , and the Swedish Prime Minister, \uc2 Magdalena Andersson\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 12:47\par \par \uc2 EU Parliament\uc2  asks to consider Moldova's accession to the blocMoldovan President \uc2 Maia Sandu\uc2  spoke to the \uc2 European Parliament\uc2  on Wednesday . Photo: AFP/John Thys.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Parliament\uc2  approved a draft that accepts Moldova's application for accession to the \uc2 European Union\uc2  and asks the European institutions to recognize it as a candidate country.\par \par \uc2 The text, approved by 512 votes in favor, 43 against and 39 abstentions, states that Moldova "is on the right track for the adoption of key reforms." The approval came the day after Moldovan President \uc2 Maia Sandu\uc2  addressed MEPs, claiming her country as part of Europe and calling for its inclusion in the EU.\par \par \uc2 To support Moldova, which received more than 450 thousand Ukrainian refugees and suffers from rising energy prices, the \uc2 European Parliament\uc2  asks the \uc2 EU\uc2  for "new macro-financial assistance, transport and trade liberalization measures, and support for refugee management."\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 12:32\par \par \uc2 At least 12 killed by Russian shelling in SeverodonetskAt least 12 people were killed and 40 wounded in Russian shelling in the eastern Ukrainian city of Severodonetsk, over which Russian troops are trying to close the encirclement, the regional governor reported.\par \par \uc2 The Russians "started shelling in the morning with heavy weapons, randomly. The shelling is continuing," the governor, Sergey Gaidai, said in Telegram.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 12:15\par \par \uc2 Ukraine war puts surrogacy business and unborn babies in troubleUkraine is the European center of the surrogacy "industry". Foreign couples can take the baby they hired while in the country for only a month, even just a few weeks now in times of war, for prices starting from 39,900 euros, of which the surrogate mothers receive less than half.\par \par \uc2 According to the director of the gestational clinic that EFE visits in Kiev, Igor Petrovich, the expectant mothers are usually women without economic resources who use the money from the "program" (this is how they call gestation) to pay for renovations in their homes, care for their children or simply get by. Read more\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 11:56\par \par \uc2 NATO\uc2 : Russian offensive in Donbas is "stalled"NATO Secretary General spoke about the Russian stalemate in the Donbas. Photo: AFP/Martin Sylvest.\par \par \uc2 NATO\uc2  Secretary General \uc2 Jens Stoltenberg\uc2  said Thursday that Russia's offensive in the Donbas, the second phase of its invasion of Ukraine, is stalled\par \par \uc2 "Russia did not achieve its objectives in Ukraine: it had to abandon Kiev and Kharkov, and the offensive in the Donbas is stalled. But we do not believe that Moscow has given up its plans, so we should prepare to support Ukraine in the medium and long term," said Stoltenberg.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 11:45\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 : "The war in Europe was a distant memory".The war in Ukraine has once again placed the issue of the conflict at the heart of Europe, where it already seemed "a distant memory," \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  maintained Thursday as he received new ambassadors to the Holy See.\par \par \uc2 "After having experienced the devastating effects of two world wars, and the nuclear threats of the cold war, and a growing respect for the role of law (...) most people believed that war in Europe was a distant memory," Francis said.\par \par \uc2 The Pope lamented "the dark cloud of war that has fallen over Eastern Europe," but warned that "it is necessary not to forget that there are numerous ongoing conflicts in other parts of the world."\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 11:25\par \par \uc2 Italy proposes at the \uc2 United Nations\uc2  a gradual plan to achieve peace in UkraineItalian Chancellor \uc2 Luigi Di Maio\uc2  presented the plan at the \uc2 UN\uc2 . Photo: EFE/Georg Wendt...\par \par \uc2 Italy, through its Chancellor \uc2 Luigi Di Maio\uc2 , delivered to \uc2 UN\uc2  Secretary General \uc2 Ant\u243\'00\'F3nio Guterres\uc2  a four-step plan to restore peace in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 In its first point, the plan drawn up by the \uc2 Italian Foreign Ministry\uc2  foresees a ceasefire, which "should be accompanied by mechanisms of supervision and demilitarization of the front line", the Italian newspaper La Repubblica published in its digital version. The second point is the neutrality of Ukraine, which has to be backed by an international political "guarantee" and will be discussed within the framework of a peace conference.\par \par \uc2 The territorial issue, which envisages the status of the Crimean peninsula and the Donbas region, constitutes the third section of the Italian plan, while the last part proposes to elaborate a new multilateral agreement on peace and security in Europe.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 11:06\par \par \uc2 More Ukrainian soldiers surrendered at Mariupol steelworksUkrainian soldiers who have surrendered were sent to a prison campon. Photo: \uc2 Russian Defense Ministry\uc2  press service via AP.\par \par \uc2 Russia announced Thursday that a total of 1,730 Ukrainian servicemen who were entrenched at the Azovstal steelworks in Mariupol surrendered this week, following a battle that has become emblematic in this war that has been raging for nearly three months.\par \par \uc2 About 1,000 fighters were taken to a prison camp on Ukrainian soil under Russian control in the Donetsk region. Read more\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 10:49\par \par \uc2 Fresh shelling left 10 civilians dead in DonbasA man removes objects from a house destroyed by shelling in Donetsk. Photo: AP/Alexei Alexandrov.\par \par \uc2 Ten civilians were killed and seven others wounded in two towns in Ukraine's Donetsk region, part of the Donbas, in shelling by the Russian military in recent hours, the head of the regional military administration, Pavlo Kyrylenko, told Interfax Ukraine on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "On May 18 the Russians killed ten civilians in the Donbas, seven in Lyman and three in Bakhmut. Among the dead were two children. Another seven people were wounded today," Kyrylenko said, adding that "it is impossible to establish the exact number of victims in the occupied towns of Mariupol and Volnovakha."\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 10:28\par \par \uc2 Russia will reopen Ukrainian ports only if sanctions are liftedRussia will reopen access to Ukrainian ports, whose blockade threatens to provoke a global food crisis, only if Western countries lift sanctions against Russian exports\par \par \uc2 Russian Deputy Foreign Minister \uc2 Andrei Rudenko\uc2  told the Interfax agency that the first cause of the food crisis is "the sanctions imposed on Russia by the United States and the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , which hinder freedom of trade, particularly in foodstuffs such as wheat, feritilizers and others."\par \par \uc2 "Therefore, if our partners want a solution, it is necessary to solve the problems connected with the lifting of restrictions imposed on Russian exports," the deputy foreign minister added.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 10:11\par \par \uc2 Prosecutor's office demands life imprisonment for Russian soldier tried for war crimesThe Ukrainian prosecutor's office asked for a life sentence for the Russian soldier on trial for shooting a 62-year-old man in the head through his car window in Sumy, a village in northeastern Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Private Vadim Shishimarin, during the trial against him, testified that he acted on orders from a superior who insisted that the man, who was talking on a cell phone, might be divulging his location to others.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 09:56\par \par \uc2 George Bush wanted to condemn Russia, but confused the war in Ukraine with the one in IraqFormer President \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2  made a mistake in condemning Russia. Photo: Reuters/Kevin Lamarque/file photo.\par \par \uc2 Former U.S. President George Bush made an unusual "gaffe" that is sure to haunt him for a while: he called the Russian invasion of Iraq "totally unjustified and brutal," although he quickly rectified himself and said he was talking about Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 In a speech on Wednesday, Bush, 75, seemed to realize what he had said and after correcting himself quietly added "Iraq too," which drew laughter from the audience. Read more\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 09:40\par \par \uc2 Parliament calls for special court for Russian crimes in Ukraine The \uc2 European Parliament\uc2  on Thursday came out in favor of establishing a special international tribunal to try the "crime of aggression perpetrated against Ukraine by the political leadership and military commanders of Russia and its allies."\par \par \uc2 MEPs believe that since the \uc2 International Criminal Court\uc2  has no jurisdiction over the crime of aggression in this situation (because neither Ukraine nor the Russian Federation has ratified the Rome Statute), "this lacuna should be addressed by setting up a special international tribunal."\par \par \uc2 The deputies called on the European institutions "to support the creation without delay of an appropriate legal basis (...) to enable the establishment of this tribunal" and to provide "all the human and budgetary resources and administrative, investigative and logistical support necessary for the establishment of this tribunal."\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 09:19\par \par \uc2 UK sanctions major Russian airlines \uc2 Aeroflot\uc2  is one of the airlines sanctioned by the UK. Photo credit: Reuters/Maxim Shemetov/File image.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 British government\uc2  announcedon Thursday imposed new sanctions against major Russian airlines, including \uc2 Aeroflot\uc2 , banning them from reselling their slots in retaliation for the invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Aeroflot\uc2 , \uc2 Ural Airlines\uc2  and \uc2 Rossiya Airlines\uc2  will not be allowed to sell their slots - which they are no longer allowed to use at British airports - estimated at \u163\'00\'A350 million ($62 million), it said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The UK had already closed its airspace to Russian aircraft shortly after the invasion of Ukraine on February 24, as well as its ports to Russian ships, and had banned the export of goods and technology to the Russian air sector.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 08:50\par \par \uc2 Kremlin sees no progress in negotiations with Ukraine."The talks in fact are not progressing. And we note a complete lack of desire on the part of Ukrainian negotiators to continue this process," Russian presidential spokesman Dmitry Peskov said Thursday at his daily telephone press briefing.\par \par \uc2 The spokesman's words confirm what was stated earlier by Russian Deputy Foreign Minister \uc2 Andrei Rudenko\uc2 , who said that his country is ready to resume negotiations if Ukraine expresses its readiness to do so,\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 08:20\par \par \uc2 Red Cross searches prisoners in AzovstalAn aerial view of damaged residential buildings and the Azovstal steel plant in the background in the port city of Mariupol. AFP Photo.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Committee of the Red Cross\uc2  (Cicr) began registering prisoners of war evacuated from the Azovstal steel mill, including the wounded, at the request of both sides, the Committee said in a note detailing that it has so far registered "hundreds" of them.The registration \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  began on Tuesday and continued today. The recognition process includes a module with personal data, such as date of birth and next of kin.? "This information allows Cicr to follow those who have been captured and help them to remain in contact with their families," the note states. The question remains as to where the Ukrainian prisoners are taken once they have been registered.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 07:59\par \par \uc2 First Russian soldier tried in Ukraine for war crimes asks for "forgiveness". Russian soldier Vadim Shishimarin arrives for the opening of his war crimes trial for killing a civilian, at the Solomyansky district court in Kiev . AFP photo.\par \par \uc2 The first soldier on trial in Ukraine for war crimes asked for "forgiveness" Thursday before a Kiev court as he detailed how he killed a civilian at the start of the Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 "I know you won't be able to forgive me, but I ask for forgiveness anyway," 21-year-old Russian sergeant Vadim Shishimarin told the wife of the 62-year-old man he admitted killing in northeastern Ukraine on February 28.\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 07:37\par \par \uc2 Russia confirms readiness to resume negotiations with UkraineDeputy Foreign Minister \uc2 Andrei Rudenko\uc2  and other officials during one of the negotiation rounds. AP Photo.\par \par \uc2 Russia is ready to resume negotiations with Ukraine if Kiev expresses its readiness to do so, Russian Deputy Foreign Minister \uc2 Andrei Rudenko\uc2  said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "It was not us who interrupted the negotiation process, it was paused by our Ukrainian partners. As soon as they express readiness to return to the negotiating table, we will naturally respond in the affirmative," he told the Russian press, quoted by the Interfax agency.\par \par \uc2 According to the Russian top diplomat, "the important thing is that there is something to talk about". The day before the Kremlin stated that at the moment negotiations between Moscow and Kiev are completely stopped due to Ukraine's "absolute unwillingness".\par \par \uc2 19.05.2022\par \par \uc2 07:20\par \par \uc2 Turkey said it will say "no" to Sweden, Finland in NATOTurkish President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  addresses members of his ruling AK Party (AKP) during a meeting in parliament in Ankara, Turkey. Reuters photo.\par \par \uc2 In a speech to a group of young Turks, Turkey's President Recep \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  accused the two Nordic nations, especially Sweden, of being a "hotbed of terror, the home of terror''. The video of the conversation was made public on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Erdogan's objections stem from Turkey's complaints that Stockholm, and to a lesser extent Helsinki, would support the outlawed \uc2 Kurdistan Workers' Party\uc2 , or \uc2 PKK\uc2 , and an armed group in Syria that Ankara considers an extension of \uc2 the PKK\uc2 . It also accuses them of harboring followers of U.S.-based Muslim cleric Fethullah Gulen, whom the country blames for being behind a 2016 coup attempt.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's yes is crucial for Sweden and Finland's membership in the military alliance because the decision must be unanimous. Each of its 30 members can veto the entry of other candidates.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220520ei5k006mb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
