\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 European unity breaks down: Italy's \uc2 ENI\uc2  opens ruble account to pay for gas\b0\par\par\uc2 679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Italian hydrocarbons company \uc2 ENI\uc2 , 30% controlled by the Italian Treasury, has begun the formalities for opening a ruble account at \uc2 Gazprombank\uc2 , as a "precautionary measure" and "in view of the imminent expiration of the deadline for payment expected in the next few days", the company announced. In this way, the European unity in the face of the sanctions is broken by one of the most important countries.\par \par \uc2 ENI\uc2  has initiated the opening "of the two current accounts named K, one in euros and the other in rubles, indicated by \uc2 Gazprom Export\uc2 , in accordance with a unilateral claim to modify the existing contracts, in line with the new gas payment procedure ordered by the Russian Federation", it said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 However, the Italian group clarifies that "it has long rejected these changes" and that , "therefore, the opening of the accounts is on a temporary basis and without prejudice to the contractual rights of the company, which provide for the fulfillment of the obligation to pay in euros."\par \par \uc2 "This express reservation will also accompany the execution of the corresponding payments," the company adds. Close sources told Efe a few days ago that \uc2 ENI\uc2  intended to open an account in rubles to fulfill the Russian gas payment commitment and that it was waiting to see if the European authorities would make it clear with a regulation that paying in rubles, as demanded by Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , is not allowed.\par \par \uc2 "The decision, shared with Italian institutions, was taken in compliance with the framework of international sanctions and in the context of ongoing discussions with \uc2 Gazprom Export\uc2  to expressly confirm the allocation to \uc2 Gazprom Export\uc2  itself of any possible costs or risks associated with the different way of executing the payment," \uc2 ENI\uc2  explained in its note.\par \par \uc2 Italian Prime Minister \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  said last week in the United States - where he traveled for talks with President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on the situation in Ukraine - that "most of the European importers" of Russian gas have already "opened their accounts in rubles" and assured that \uc2 ENI\uc2  would pay on time, although he did not specify whether it would do so in euros or rubles, and reiterated that the \uc2 European Union\uc2  (\uc2 EU\uc2 ) has not officially indicated what to do about this situation.\par \par \uc2 "On the one hand, to date, \uc2 Gazprom Export\uc2  and the competent Russian federal authorities have confirmed that the invoicing (effectively received by \uc2 ENI\uc2  in recent days in the contractually correct \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) and the corresponding payment by \uc2 ENI\uc2  will continue to be executed in euros, as foreseen in the contract."\par \par \uc2 Also "that the \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities of conversion from euros to rubles will be performed by a special clearing agent operating on the Moscow Stock Exchange within 48 hours from the credit and without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 " and that, "in case of delays or technical impossibility to complete the conversion within the foreseen deadlines, it will not have any impact on the supplies".\par \par \uc2 "On the other hand, the execution of payments in this way does not find for now any European regulatory provision that foresees prohibitions directly affecting the possibility of executing these \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," adds the Italian company.\par \par \uc2 ENI\uc2  stresses that the new procedure "is not incompatible with the existing sanctioning framework and its compliance occurs at the time of the transfer of the euros."\par \par \uc2 "A failure to pay would expose \uc2 ENI\uc2  both to the risk of non-compliance with the obligation to fulfill in good faith any contractual request from \uc2 Gazprom Export\uc2  imposed by its own authority, and to the risk posed to \uc2 Eni\uc2  of non-compliance with sales commitments to downstream customers in the event of supply disruption," it adds.\par \par \uc2 However, \uc2 ENI\uc2  "in the absence of future full, comprehensive and contractually substantiated responses by \uc2 Gazprom Export\uc2 , will initiate international arbitration on the basis of Swedish law (as provided for in existing contracts) to resolve doubts regarding the contractual changes required by the new payment procedure and the correct allocation of costs and risks."\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220518ei5i0071j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
