\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war, live: Pope calls for Easter truce, says invasion "crucifies Christ again"\b0\par\par\uc2 5,016 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 LIVENews in DevelopmentOnSunday, \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  called for a truce in Ukraine, where "Christ is being crucified again". He said this during the Palm Sunday Mass in St. Peter's Square.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, echoes of the surprise visit of the British Prime Minister, \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , to Kiev, where he met with President \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2 , continue.\par \par \uc2 During the meeting, he confirmed that he will deliver 120 armored vehicles and anti-ship missile systems\par \par \uc2 to the Ukrainian armed forces. In addition, he announced a new funding package of $500 million (\u8364\'20\'AC460 million) for Ukraine through the \uc2 World Bank.10.04.2022\par \par \uc2 07:53\par \par \uc2 Pope calls for Easter truce in UkrainePope Francis said today that in the war in Ukraine Christ is being crucified again and called for an "Easter truce" to start real negotiations and "come to peace," as he celebrated Palm Sunday Mass at the Vatican.\par \par \uc2 "When violence is used, one no longer knows anything about God, who is Father, nor about others, who are brothers," the Pope lamented during the ceremony he led in St. Peter's Square and which marks the beginning of Vatican celebrations for Easter.\par \par \uc2 10.04.2022\par \par \uc2 06:05\par \par \uc2 Russia confirmed attacks in Dnipropetrovsk regionTheDefense Ministry of the Russian Federation confirmed that it destroyed a Ukrainian nationalist battalion headquarters and base in the village of Zvonetskoye, Dnipropetrovsk region, with high-precision missiles\par \par \uc2 .Valentyn Reznichenko, head of the Dnipropetrovsk regional military administration, also gave an account of different attacks in the region over the past day. "There were sirens almost every hour. And, unfortunately, there are incoming shells in different areas," he said in statements picked up by CNN.\par \par \uc2 Russia also reported "high-precision air-launched missiles in the area of the village of Starobogdanovka, Mykolaiv region and the Chuguev military airfield," with which it destroyed "launchers of Ukrainian S-300 anti-aircraft missile systems identified by reconnaissance."\par \par \uc2 10.04.2022\par \par \uc2 05:41\par \par \uc2 Another mass grave with dead civilians found, in KievThechairman of the Dmitrov community, Taras Didych, revealed the discovery of a new mass grave with more dead civilians near the town of Buzova, Kiev region\par \par \uc2 ."Near the Buzova gas station we have found more dead in a grave, civilians," he indicated on television, as picked up by the Unian agency. In addition, he maintained that on the road linking the Ukrainian capital with Zhitomir, between the villages of Myla and Mriya, a dozen cars were shot at.\par \par \uc2 "In the community there are 14 villages, some of which were under occupation. Now we are returning to life, but during the occupation we had our 'hot spots', many civilians were killed," he said.\par \par \uc2 10.04.2022\par \par \uc2 05:17\par \par \uc2 Ukraine agreed on nine humanitarian corridors for thisSundayUkraine'\par \par \uc2 sDeputy Prime Minister \uc2 Iryna Vereshchuk\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian Deputy Prime Minister \uc2 Iryna Vereshchuk\uc2  confirmed that Kiev agreed to implement nine humanitarian corridors to allow citizens of her country to escape from some of the areas most affected by the war with Russia, such as Donetsk and Lugansk.\par \par \uc2 "All routes of humanitarian corridors in the Luhansk region will work as long as there is a ceasefire by the Russian occupation troops," Vereshchuk said in a statement released via his Telegram channel.\par \par \uc2 10.04.2022\par \par \uc2 05:00\par \par \uc2 Russia bringing in off-duty military personnel from 2012, UK saysInresponse to the high number of casualties suffered by Russian troops in Ukraine, the Kremlin is recruiting off-duty military personnel from 2012 to boost its ranks, the \uc2 UK Ministry of Defense\uc2  said Sunday\par \par \uc2 .The Russian armed forces are also trying to recruit soldiers in the Moldovan region of Transinistria, separated from the rest of the country by the Dniester River and self-proclaimed independent, adds the intelligence information released by Defense on its official \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account.\par \par \uc2 Western countries estimate that between 7,000 and 15,000 Russian servicemen have died since the Kremlin-ordered invasion began.\par \par \uc2 10.04.2022\par \par \uc2 04:27\par \par \uc2 EU\uc2  backed Ukraine: 'It will rise even stronger'Josep Borrell Fontelles, High Representative of the European Union for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy, openly expressed his support for Ukraine on Sunday\par \par \uc2 ."Ukraine will prevail and will rise even stronger. And the \uc2 EU\uc2  will continue to stand by its side every step of the way. Glory to Ukraine!" he posted on his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account.\par \par \uc2 10.04.2022\par \par \uc2 02:47\par \par \uc2 Since the beginning of the Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  177 children died in UkraineSincethe beginning of the full-scale invasion of the Russian Federation in Ukraine, 177 children have died and 336 have been injured, the Prosecutor General's Office reported on Sunday\par \par \uc2 ."According to the data received by juvenile prosecutors, 177 children were killed and more than 336 were injured," it specified.\par \par \uc2 10.04.2022\par \par \uc2 02:38\par \par \uc2 Russian troops fired on a school and two buildings inLuganskRussian forces on Sunday attacked a school and two multi-storey buildings in Severodonetsk, Lugansk region, with no casualties reported in the early hours, the head of the regional military administration, Serhiy Gaidai\par \par \uc2 , said."The enemy shelling took place in the morning of April 10. At one of the entrances, apartments from the first to the fifth floor were burned to the ground. Firefighters located the fire and evacuated two people who had lived there since 1938. Another missile hit three other apartments. Fortunately, there were no casualties. The building of one of the nearby schools was also damaged," Gaidai said.\par \par \uc2 He also said that two houses in Lisichansk and Kamyshevakh were destroyed in another attack on Saturday night.\par \par \uc2 10.04.2022\par \par \uc2 02:02\par \par \uc2 Lithuanian documentary filmmaker killed in Mariupol allegedly tortured by Russian troops Lithuanian film director and documentary filmmaker Mantas Kvedaravicius, who died in the Ukrainian city of Mariupol in southeastern Ukraine a week ago, was captured and tortured by Russian troops, Ukrainian lawmaker Andrii Osadchuk revealed\par \par \uc2 .The 45-year-old director's death was announced by fellow Russian-Latvian Vitalijus Manskis, who wrote on his \uc2 Facebook\uc2  account that Kvedaravicius died "with the camera in his hands." It was initially reported that he had been hit by a missile.\par \par \uc2 However, this Sunday, Osadchuk denounced "the brutal execution of Lithuanian film director Mantas Kvedaravicius in Mariupol by Russian troops." "We will never forget, we will never forgive the Russians," he expressed.\par \par \uc2 The Lithuanian was known precisely for a documentary film called "Mariupolis" (2016), which focused on the experiences of the inhabitants of the port city, to reflect the conflict in eastern Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 10.04.2022\par \par \uc2 01:36\par \par \uc2 Zelenski thanked \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  and the United KingdomThePresident of Ukraine, \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2 , expressed his gratitude towards Great Britain and its Prime Minister, \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , for the support provided to his country in the framework of the war conflict it has been maintaining with Russia since last February 24\par \par \uc2 ."Boris was among those who did not hesitate for a minute whether to support Ukraine. The leadership of Great Britain in providing our country with defense assistance and also leadership in the policy of sanctions will remain forever in history," the Ukrainian president said in his evening speech on social networks.\par \par \uc2 He added that "Ukraine will always be grateful to Boris and Great Britain for this". Johnson, made a surprise visit to Ukraine this Saturday, during which he announced to Zelenski the new shipment of armaments and economic aid.\par \par \uc2 "The other democratic Western countries should follow the example of the UK," the Ukrainian president suggested.\par \par \uc2 10.04.2022\par \par \uc2 01:03\par \par \uc2 Protest against the invasion of Ukraine, in front of the Russian embassy in Santiago, ChileThedemonstration gathered dozens of people in the Chilean capital. Photo AP Photo/Esteban FelixDozens of\par \par \uc2 demonstrators stationed themselves Saturday in front of the Russian embassy in Santiago, Chile, in order to show their disagreement with the Kremlin troops' invasion of Ukraine\par \par \uc2 .The large group of people, including Ukrainians living in Chile, unfurled a huge banner with the colors of the European country's flag.\par \par \uc2 Some demonstrators even lay down on the ground hugging stuffed animals, in tribute to the child victims of the war.\par \par \uc2 10.04.2022\par \par \uc2 00:24\par \par \uc2 Ukraine definitively banned the import of products from RussiaUkraineconfirmed "the complete cessation of trade in goods" with Russia and informed that "no products" from that country "may be imported" to its territory. This was announced by the Ukrainian Minister of Economic Development and Trade \uc2 Yulia Svyrydenko\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to estimates of the \uc2 Ukrainian Ministry of Economy\uc2 , this resolution will entail the blockade of about 6 billion dollars a year in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Russia. "The enemy's budget will not receive these funds, which will reduce its potential to finance the war," the official statement argued.\par \par \uc2 "This step by Ukraine can serve as an example for our Western partners and will encourage them to strengthen sanctions against Russia," Svyrydenko's \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post expanded\par \par \uc2 .09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 23:43\par \par \uc2 Shakhtar Donetsk kicked off a "World Peace Tour" in GreeceTheUkrainian team took on Olympiacos in Greece for solidarity purposes\par \par \uc2 .Shakhtar Donetsk, one of the most popular Ukrainian soccer teams, launched a "World Peace Tour", through which it will raise funds, with ticket sales and advertising, to donate to volunteer, medical and children's organizations in its country affected by the war with Russia, as officially announced by the club.\par \par \uc2 The first stop of this solidarity mission took place in Athens, where the Ukrainian team faced Olympiacos. All the players wore T-shirts with the slogan "Stop War" and the Ukrainian players even wore on their backs, above the number, the names of ten cities that the Russian forces tried to take over.\par \par \uc2 In addition to a minute of silence in tribute to the victims of the war, 176 toys were placed in a special section of the Georgios Karaiskakis stadium in memory of the same number of children who died in Ukraine as a result of the war.\par \par \uc2 The next game of Shakhtar Donetsk's "World Peace Tour", after Saturday's 1-0 defeat, a result that is little short of anecdotal, will be played on April 14 in Gdansk, Poland, against Lechia.\par \par \uc2 09.04\par \par \uc2 .2022\par \par \uc2 22:26\par \par \uc2 Through local church, Bucha survivors finally receiveaidCivilians remaining in Bucha formed long lines Saturday to receive food gifts from the local church in the destroyed Kiev suburb, where evidence of war crimes was warned following the withdrawal of Russian forces\par \par \uc2 .Due to the flight of other civilians by the Russian invasion, most of those who remained in Bucha were elderly, poor people or those who found it impossible to leave their loved ones behind. Russian forces withdrew more than a week ago.\par \par \uc2 Volunteer Petro Denysyuk told AP that he and his fellow church members and friends began distributing food, which consisted of a wide range of groceries and hot meals.\par \par \uc2 "We gathered with the youth of our church and prepared food for the needy,'' Denysyuk said. "We prepared pilaf, boiled eggs, prepared meat, sausages and noodles.''\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 21:46\par \par \uc2 ?The curious picture of a missile falling by parachute that spread on networks09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 21:31\par \par \uc2 ?4,532 people escaped from Ukraine in the last 24 hours This was reported by Ukrainian Deputy Prime Minister \uc2 Iryna Vereshchuk\uc2 . However, she also noted that buses to evacuate Berdyansk, Tokmak and Energodar had to return because they were blocked by Russian forces. People in these cities could only flee by cars.\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 20:43\par \par \uc2 ? "We have nothing to eat", the harsh confession of a Russian soldier to his wifeThewar in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The Russian invasion in Ukraine is spreading without a clear end and \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's troops are beginning to disbelieve their leaders, amid concerns about resource shortages.\par \par \uc2 The Main Intelligence Directorate of the \uc2 Ukrainian Defense Ministry\uc2  on Saturday released the transcript of an intercepted telephone conversation between a Russian soldier and his wife, in which he tells her that he and his comrades are not being fed adequately during the military incursion into the neighboring country."They give us canned food that is impossible to eat", assures the soldier, who details that they opened one that was supposed to contain a kind of stew, with chicken, but the portion was excessively scarce.? Continue reading09\par \par \uc2 .04.2022\par \par \uc2 20:18\par \par \uc2 The moment of the explosion of a nitric acid tanker in the Ukrainian city of Mezhove09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 20:06\par \par \uc2 Rift in Russia: denunciations, threats and dismissals for thinking differentlyMarinaDubrova, an English teacher on Russia's Pacific island of Sakhalin, showed an uplifting \uc2 YouTube\uc2  video to her eighth grade class last month in which the kids, in Russian and Ukrainian, sing about a "world without war."\par \par \uc2 After she showed it, a group of girls hung back during recess and asked her about her views.\par \par \uc2 "Ukraine is a separate country, a separate one," teacher Dubrova, 57, told them. "Not anymore," one of the girls replied. Read the full story09\par \par \uc2 .04.2022\par \par \uc2 19:53\par \par \uc2 Funds from the \uc2 IMF\uc2  account to support Ukraine will be used to stabilize its economy The money available on the special account opened to support Ukraine and approved by the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  will be earmarked to stabilize the country's economy.?This was confirmed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 of that country, from where they also informed that Canada plans to send up to 1 billion Canadian dollars ($ 795 million) to it.09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 18:14\par \par \uc2 Zelenski, on negotiations with Russia: "We do not want to miss opportunities for a diplomatic solution "The President of Ukraine, \uc2 Volodomir Zelenski\uc2 , spoke about the state of talks with Russia. "Nobody wants to negotiate with a person or persons who have tortured this nation. It is understandable. And as a man, as a father, I understand it very well,'' Zelenski said.?However, he clarified, "We don't want to miss opportunities, if we have them, for a diplomatic solution\par \par \uc2 .''09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 17:50\par \par \uc2 Mariupol scenario is "ten times worse than the Bucha genocide "The Mariupol municipality assured that the scale of crimes of the Russian forces in that city "is ten times worse than the Bucha genocide". Thelocal government posted the message via Telegram, with a photo of "an underpass, in the outlying district of Sadkiv", in which bodies are seen lined up on the ground. "Here the occupants set up a collection point for the bodies of murdered residents. Hundreds of corpses are brought to these points every day\par \par \uc2 ," to then "destroy them in mobile crematoria or bury them in mass graves," they detailed. "09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 17:46\par \par \uc2 Images of \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  and Volodimir Zelenski09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 16:14\par \par \uc2 Canada increases humanitarian aid for UkraineTheCanadian prime minister took part in the Stand Up for Ukraine campaign. Photo: AFP/Janek Skarzynski.\par \par \uc2 Canada on Saturday announced measures to facilitate the arrival of Ukrainian refugees and pledged an additional C$100 million (US$79.5 million) in aid to Ukraine and neighboring countries.\par \par \uc2 These additional funds were announced during the Stand Up for Ukraine international fundraiser by Canadian Prime Minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2 . "We continue our efforts to facilitate the arrival of Ukrainians in Canada," Trudeau said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 15:55\par \par \uc2 Radioactive contamination rises at ChernobylThelatest measurements showed an increase in radioactive contamination at Chernobyl.... Photo credit: Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine reported on Saturday an increase in the level of radioactive contamination at the former Chernobyl nuclear power plant, although it indicated that it remains within the usual limits, reported the \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2  (\uc2 IAEA\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 This \uc2 UN\uc2  agency noted that the Ukrainian authorities are gradually re-establishing nuclear and radiological safety control.\par \par \uc2 In a new situation report to the \uc2 IAEA\uc2 , Ukraine referred to an "increase in the level of radioactive contamination (...) due to non-compliance with radiation safety requirements and strict access procedures", although it assured that radiation remains "within limits" at this facility, where in 1986 the worst nuclear accident in history took place\par \par \uc2 .09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 15:30\par \par \uc2 General Dvornikov to be new commander ofRussian forces in Ukraine Russian forces have suffered losses and had to withdraw from several regions. Photo: AP/Felipe Dana.\par \par \uc2 Alexander Dvornikov, a veteran awarded in 2015 with the title of "Hero of the Russian Federation" for leading the Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Syria, was appointed as the new commander of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's military \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine,\par \par \uc2 Dvornikov comes to the command as part of a change in strategy, a senior official who asked to remain anonymous confirmed to the \uc2 BBC\uc2 . "Dvornikov has enormous experience of Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Syria. We expect him to improve the coordination of Russian forces in Ukraine," he said.\par \par \uc2 For international analysts, Dvornikov's appointment is evidence of Moscow's frustrations after fierce month-and-a-half-long fighting failed to yield the results the Kremlin had hoped for.\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 15:15\par \par \uc2 Ukraine finalized a new prisoner exchange with RussiaUkraine announced on Saturday that it carried out the "third exchange" of prisoners with Russia, leading to the release of 12 Ukrainian soldiers and 14 Ukrainian civilians.\par \par \uc2 "By order of President (\uc2 Volodimir) Zelensky\uc2 , the third prisoner exchange took place today. Twelve of our soldiers are returning home, including a female officer. We have also allowed the release of 14 civilians, including nine women," Ukrainian Deputy Prime Minister \uc2 Iryna Vereshchuk\uc2  said on Telegram.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine conducted its first prisoner swap with Russia in late March, when ten Russian soldiers were exchanged for ten Ukrainian servicemen and eleven Russian civilian sailors for 19 Ukrainian civilians. On April 1, Ukraine reported the release of 86 of its servicemen captured by Russia in an exchange for Russian servicemen whose number was not specified.\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 15:00\par \par \uc2 A story about the horrors of the war The horrors of the war in Ukraine continue to shock. This week the story came out of a woman who was raped for a week by a Russian soldier who, in an argument, killed her elderly mother in front of her eyes for refusing to run away with him.\par \par \uc2 The heinous story was told by Vira, a friend of the victim, on her \uc2 Facebook\uc2  profile. It was then picked up by the War in Ukraine site, an online archive created by the Kiev government to document Russian war crimes. Read more\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 14:40\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  promises Ukraine 120 armored vehicles and anti-ship missilesPrime Minister Johnson arrived in Kiev on Saturday and met with Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2 . Photo: EFE.\par \par \uc2 The Prime Minister of the United Kingdom, \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , announced Saturday after meeting in Kiev with the President of Ukraine, \uc2 Volodymir Zelenski\uc2 , that his country will deliver 120 armored vehicles and anti-ship missile systems to the Ukrainian armed forces.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 British government\uc2  also announced a new funding package of $500 million (\u8364\'20\'AC460 million) for Ukraine through the \uc2 World Bank\uc2 , bringing the total amount of funds committed through this channel to $1 billion (\u8364\'20\'AC920 million).\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 14:15\par \par \uc2 Another mass grave with corpses of Russian soldiers discoveredThe Ukrainian Army found a mass grave with Russian soldiers in Viljivka, outside Kharkov, just over a week after the discovery of mass graves and bodies of executed civilians in Bucha.\par \par \uc2 "Finally the myth that Russians do not leave their dead behind is destroyed. During the cleanup of the locality of Vilkhivka near Kharkov, a mass grave of occupying soldiers has been discovered," the Armed Forces Strategic Communication Department reported on its \uc2 Facebook\uc2  account.\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 13:50\par \par \uc2 Pope's envoy to take ambulance donated by Vatican to KievPolish Cardinal Konrad Krajewski, the Pope's alms donor, will leave on Sunday again for Ukraine, where he will carry a second ambulance gifted by Francis.\par \par \uc2 It is the third time that the cardinal alms-giver has gone to the war-torn country, passing through Poland, but this time the destination is Kiev. The aim is not only to deliver a second ambulance, but also to celebrate the Easter Triduum in the Ukrainian capital, remaining in the country throughout Holy Week.\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 13:29\par \par \uc2 Russian soldiers contaminated at Chernobyl have one year to live View of the Chernobyl nuclear power plant from the ghost town of Pripyat, Photo: Reuters/Gleb Garanich.\par \par \uc2 A Ukrainian engineer at the Chernobyl nuclear power plant said that Russian soldiers not only dug trenches in a highly contaminated area, but also committed careless actions, such as touching radioactive material with unprotected bare hands.\par \par \uc2 Valeriy Simyonov, the plant's chief safety engineer, told \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  that a Russian soldier even picked up a source of cobalt-60 with his bare hands and without gloves.\par \par \uc2 For his part, Energy Minister German Galushchenko said that the Russian soldiers who dug the trenches near the power plant are no more than a year old, the \uc2 Ukrainian Defense Ministry\uc2  posted on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 13:11\par \par \uc2 Julio Alga\u241\'00\'F1araz\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's real reasons for launching the invasion of Ukraine.Russian army soldiers aboard a BTR-80 armored personnel carrier transit a Ukrainian road. Photo: EFE/ Stringer\par \par \uc2 For British historian Donald Sasson, the rupture of the 70 years of peace that Europe has experienced "is the most serious mistake made since then by a European leader."\par \par \uc2 For Sergei Karaganov, a close advisor to Putin and Russian Foreign Minister \uc2 Sergei Lavrov\uc2 , "the real war is against Western expansionism", and argues that "the conflict was becoming probable. We saw the deep divisions and structural problems in Western societies. We decided to strike first." Read more\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 12:49\par \par \uc2 Russia blames the West for "more bloodshed."The West's arms supply to Ukraine causes "more bloodshed," and may lead "the United States and the Russian Federation down the path of direct military confrontation," Russian Ambassador to the United States \uc2 Anatoly Antonov\uc2  said in an interview with Newsweek\par \par \uc2 "Western states are directly involved in the current events as they continue to flood Ukraine with weapons and ammunition, thus inciting further bloodshed," the Russian diplomat added.\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 12:30\par \par \uc2 Artificial intelligence used to identify perpetrators of Ukrainian massacresBucha was the scene of one of the largest massacres of civilians in Ukraine. Photo: AFP/Ronaldo Schemidt.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian Deputy Prime Minister and head of Digital Transformation, Myjailo Fedorov, assured that facial recognition technology and artificial intelligence already made it possible to find and identify many of the perpetrators of the killings in Bucha and Irpin.\par \par \uc2 "Today, technology makes it possible to find everyone who has been caught at least once by a target. And taking into account how much they like to post photos on the Internet and the number of cameras in cities and houses, we will solve this issue very quickly," Fedorov was quoted as saying by the Unian agency.\par \par \uc2 The official specified that "many murderers who terrorized civilians in Bucha and Irpen have already been found (...) In a short time, we will establish all information about these people: their profiles in social networks, where and with whom they serve and live."\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 12:15\par \par \uc2 Global collection raises $11 billion for Ukrainian refugeesVolodimir Zelenski joined by video call the conference where the amount raised was announced. Photo: AFP/Janek Skarzynski.\par \par \uc2 A global fundraising campaign to help Ukrainians who are refugees or displaced by the Russian invasion raised 10.1 billion euros ($11 billion), \uc2 European Commission\uc2  President \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  said Saturday in Warsaw.\par \par \uc2 The Stand Up For Ukraine campaign "raised 9.1 billion euros for people, inside and outside Ukraine, who fled the bombs, and the \uc2 EBRD\uc2  (\uc2 European Bank for Reconstruction and Development\uc2 ) pledged 1 billion more," \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 11:55\par \par \uc2 Death toll in Bucha rises to 360 civiliansMilitary and police personnel continue to collect data and search for dead bodies of civilians in Bucha. Photo: AP/Rodrigo Abd.\par \par \uc2 Authorities in Bucha have so far counted 360 civilians killed in that city, including at least 10 children, Ukrainian parliament human rights commissioner \uc2 Lyudmyla Denisova\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The official posted this on Telegram, where she also noted the Russians "shot people in the face, burned their eyes, cut off body parts and tortured adults and children to death."\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 11:40\par \par \uc2 Italy to reopen embassy in Kiev after EasterIn a gesture of strong support for Ukraine and its people, Italy plans to reopen its embassy in Kiev at the end of April or in the first days of May, it was officially announced, after being forced to move it to Lviv in the face of the Russian advance.\par \par \uc2 "We were the last to leave Kiev and we will be among the first to return," Italian Foreign Minister \uc2 Luigi Di Maio\uc2  told the Crisis Unit together with Italian Ambassador to Ukraine Francesco Zazo, in connection from Lviv, and Ambassador Giorgio Starace, from Moscow.\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 11:17\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  met with Zelenski on surprise visit to KievBritish Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  met in Kiev with Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2 . Photo: \uc2 Facebook\uc2 /Andrij Sybiha.\par \par \uc2 British Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  on Saturday paid a surprise visit to Ukraine during which he met in Kiev with President \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2 , an aide to the Ukrainian leader said.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 's visit to Kiev has just begun with a meeting with President Zelenski," the aide, Andriy Sybiha, said in a message posted on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  next to a photo of the two leaders.\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 10:49\par \par \uc2 Russian shelling has completely destroyed 21 clinics in UkraineUkrainian soldiers inside the Mariupol maternity hospital shelled by Russian forces. Photo: AP/Evgeniy Maloletka.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian Health Minister Viktor Lyashko reported Saturday that Russian shelling has damaged a total of 307 health facilities, with 21 clinics completely destroyed, and stressed the need to deploy field hospitals.\par \par \uc2 The official noted that, depending on the degree of destruction in hospitals, doctors are frequently moved from one intact building to another. And he added that many patients have been evacuated from Donetsk and Luhansk regions to safer places.\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 10:23\par \par \uc2 Ukraine creates online archive to document Russian war crimesThe \uc2 Ukrainian Foreign Ministry\uc2  on Saturday announced the creation of an online archive to document war crimes committed by Russia in Ukraine with evidence that will help ensure that their perpetrators do not escape justice.\par \par \uc2 "We thoroughly document every atrocity, every crime. We have created a special online archive of these crimes to let the world know the truth and to hold the Russians accountable for every drop of Ukrainian blood they shed," Ukrainian Foreign Minister \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "We will punish Russian war criminals for the atrocities they are committing in Ukraine, not only the executors, but also the commanders who gave the orders and the entire military-political leadership of the Russian Federation," the minister said.\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 10:05\par \par \uc2 Zelensky says Ukraine remains "ready" to negotiate with RussiaZelensky expressed Ukrainian willingness to continue negotiations with Russia. Photo: Reuters/Valentyn Ogirenko.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine remains "ready" to negotiate with Russia, although talks have been suspended since the discovery of atrocities in several cities near Kiev following the withdrawal of Russian troops, President \uc2 Volodimir Zelenski\uc2  said on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 "We are ready to fight and to seek parallel diplomatic ways to stop this war. For now we contemplate holding a dialogue in parallel," the leader said at a press conference with Austrian Chancellor \uc2 Karl Nehammer\uc2 , who is in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 09:44\par \par \uc2 Russia vows retaliation after \uc2 YouTube\uc2  channel blockingRussian authorities on Saturday accused the \uc2 YouTube\uc2  platform belonging to U.S. giant \uc2 Google\uc2  of blocking the Russian parliamentary channel and promised retaliation.\par \par \uc2 The speaker of the lower house of parliament, \uc2 Vyacheslav Volodin\uc2 , claimed that the \uc2 YouTube\uc2  channel "Duma-TV" had been blocked and denounced that with this measure the United States was violating "the rights of Russians."\par \par \uc2 "The United States wants to have a monopoly on the dissemination of information. We cannot allow it," the lawmaker said on his Telegram account. According to \uc2 Google\uc2 , the channel was shut down due to recent sanctions enacted by the \uc2 US government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 09:23\par \par \uc2 Ukraine evacuates Kramatorsk by road after attack on railway stationResidents of Kramatorsk board a minibus to leave the city. Photo: AFP/Fadel Senna.\par \par \uc2 The evacuation of civilians from Kramatorsk continued Saturday with buses and minibuses, following the attack on the local train station that left at least 50 dead and nearly 100 wounded.\par \par \uc2 A day after the bombing, civilian evacuations were continuing by highway, including dozens of survivors who spent the night in a church in the city center, not far from the attacked station.\par \par \uc2 Kramatorsk is in an area of Donetsk province not controlled by the self-proclaimed republic of the same name, a Russian-speaking region of Ukraine that took up arms against the national government eight years ago.\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 09:06\par \par \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  downgrades Russian debt to "selective default".Russia paid off dollar-denominated sovereign debt with rubles. Photo: EFE/Yuri Kochetkov.\par \par \uc2 Ratings agency S&P Global Ratings on Saturday cut Russia's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt rating to "selective default" after Moscow settled a dollar-denominated item with rubles earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 The agency downgraded the note on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt, such as the dollar, to the "SD" category and left ruble payments at the "CC" step, the rating agency said. The "SD" rating is almost the lowest on the ladder, one level above "D" which indicates a "defaut" or debt default.\par \par \uc2 "We do not believe that investors will be able to convert these payments into dollar ruble equivalents of the amounts originally due, nor that the government can convert the payments within the 30-day grace period," S&P estimated.\par \par \uc2 09.04.2022\par \par \uc2 08:45\par \par \uc2 More than 4.4 million people fled Ukraine Ukrainian refugees seek information at the central railway station in Warsaw. Photo: AP/Czarek Sokolowski.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian refugees who fled the country since the beginning of the Russian invasion have surpassed 4.4 million, \uc2 UNHCR\uc2 , the \uc2 United Nations refugee agency\uc2 , announced Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Since February 24 - the day the Russian invasion of the country began - a total of 4,441,663 citizens have left Ukraine. Such an influx of refugees is the largest for Europe since World War II.\par \par \uc2 UNHCR\uc2  further estimates that there are 7.1 million internally displaced persons in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220410ei4a004ik\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
