\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 "The resurrection of the ruble": despite the risk of default and sanctions, it is back to its pre-war level\b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Despite the sanctions imposed by the West, the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is recovering against the US dollar and is trading at levels close to those seen before the Russian invasion, a sign that the initial impact of the sanctions - one of the harshest in history - may be fading.\par \par \uc2 The ruble trades at 75.9500 per dollar, a record not seen since February 16, eight days before Russia' s first offensive into Ukraine. It is worth recalling that the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to historic lows against the US dollar, a large part of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves held by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were frozen and rating agencies downgraded Russia's credit rating to "junk bond" status. In early March, the ruble suffered its steepest decline of more than 33% against the dollar. Despite all this, the ruble managed to recover.\par \par \uc2 What measures were taken to make this happen? The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  took drastic measures to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, applying capital controls preventing investors and companies from selling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . These measures allowed Russia to maintain demand for its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The problem lies in the fact that when the restrictions are lifted, it is not guaranteed that investors will decide to buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of their own free will.\par \par \uc2 Another factor fueling demand is an increase in gas export earnings, as well as a significant drop in imports. According to Bloomberg Economics, Russia is expected to earn about $321 billion (about \u8364\'20\'AC292 billion) from its energy exports in 2022, a third more than it earned in 2021, if its big customers, including the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , continue to buy Russian oil and gas.\par \par \uc2 "Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings do not reflect the fundamentals of the Russian economy. Most of the time, those fundamentals are reflected in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But as soon as capital controls are implemented, that picture is dulled," \uc2 Craig Erlam\uc2 , senior market analyst at \uc2 OANDA\uc2 , told \uc2 DW\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "There is no way of knowing whether the Russian economy is now facing the same picture as it was in mid-February, before the invasion of Ukraine, even if the ruble seems to suggest so," he told \uc2 DW\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) predicted in January that Russia's economy would grow by 2.8% this year, it is now forecast to fall by 10-15%.\par \par \uc2 As the ruble plunged in the wake of the invasion and the ensuing Western sanctions, \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to play the role of fire extinguisher to rescue the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was falling further and further. In an attempt to save it, the financial institution doubled the benchmark interest rate to 20%, restricted domestic companies' access to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and set limits on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  withdrawals. It also took measures to prevent dollar flight, including a ban on investors dumping Russian stocks and bonds.\par \par \uc2 "Effectively, he's just artificially propping up the ruble, while appearing to be forcing buyers in hostile countries to use that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Erlam explained. "That's similar to the measures that have already been imposed on \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  bank, and other Russian banks, in terms of forcing them to convert 80% of their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  payments into rubles. This further supports those kinds of desperate measures."\par \par \uc2 Despite this rally,the outlook for the ruble looks less positive in the long term. The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - which has weakened markedly against the dollar over the past two decades - is expected to continue to struggle to re-emerge as the West looks to move swiftly away from Russian oil and gas, the lifelines of Moscow's economy.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220407ei47006bk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
