\par\par \b \uc2 As Oil Briefly Dips Below $100, Russia and Europe Play a Game of Chicken -- Barrons.com\b0\par\par\uc2 1,890 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 2022\par 12:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 U.S. oil prices briefly dipped below $100 barrel Friday, as President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's plan to release one million barrels a day of reserves began to have the desired effect.\par \par \uc2 But it's premature to start thinking it's the beginning of the end of higher prices, or even volatility.\par \par \uc2 Biden \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  where the \uc2 Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't, as the group of major oil producers stuck to its modest oil output increase for May on Thursday. If \uc2 OPEC\uc2  didn't help at $110 a barrel last month, it's safe to assume it isn't going to help at all.\par \par \uc2 The group said, perhaps significantly, that "current volatility is not caused by fundamentals, but by ongoing geopolitical developments."\par \par \uc2 That implies that the impact of Biden's massive release of oil reserves could be overshadowed in a heartbeat.\par \par \uc2 The warning signs are certainly there. Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  said on Thursday Russia will cut off gas supplies to "unfriendly" countries unless they start paying in rubles. That would spell trouble for Europe, as Russian natural gas accounted for close to 40% of the \uc2 European Union\uc2 's total gas consumption last year.\par \par \uc2 European natural-gas prices rose as a result, although gas still flowed into Europe early Friday, according to reports. It's a reminder of the delicate nature of energy markets and raises the prospect of Russia retaliating to sanctions.\par \par \uc2 While the U.S. isn't directly affected by Russia's threat, the nature of global commodities markets means one country's issue is everyone's issue. At a time of heightened inflation, the standoff is just one more worry.\par \par \uc2 -- Callum Keown\par \par \uc2 *** Join MarketWatch financial crime reporter Lukas Alpert today at noon as he talks to Ben Carlson, the director of institutional wealth management at Ritholtz Wealth Management and the author of "Don't Fall for It: A Short History of Financial Scams," about the business lessons that can be learned from some of the biggest frauds in history. Sign up here.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Biden Prods Oil Companies in Fight to Cut Fuel Prices\par \par \uc2 Biden criticized U.S. oil-and-gas companies for prioritizing shareholders over consumers, pointing to the industry's nearly $80 billion in profit last year. He announced a "use-it-or-lose-it" policy that will make oil producers pay for sitting on unused wells. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- There are 9,000 approved-but-unused drilling permits on 12 million acres \par       of federal lands, though some oil companies have announced plans to raise \par       production. Charging for unused leases would increase costs on top of \par       inflation, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tyler Glover\f28 \uc2 \f2 , CEO of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Texas Pacific Land Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par  \par    -- Biden confirmed he will release 180 million barrels of oil from the \par       Strategic Petroleum Reserve -- one million barrels a day for the next six \par       months, starting in May. The U.S. is waiting to see how much oil other \par       countries release. \par  \par    -- The price of regular unleaded gasoline averages $4.22 a gallon. Biden \par       said prices could drop 10 cents to 35 cents a gallon in coming days. \par       Andrew Lipow, president of Houston consulting firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lipow Oil Associates\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \par       told MarketWatch the savings might be between 5 and 10 cents a gallon. \par  \par    -- The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries\f28 \uc2 \f2  and allies \par       including Russia approved prior plans to increase oil output by 432,000 \par       barrels a day in May. Biden has called on \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  members to increase \par       production, while banning Russian oil imports. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What's Next: \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBC Capital Markets\f28 \uc2 \f2  found fuel demand isn't waning, despite higher prices. California Gov. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gavin Newsom\f28 \uc2 \f2  proposed $400 payments to all vehicle owners, regardless of income, for up to two cars, and Mayor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lori Lightfoot\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Chicago will distribute $150 prepaid gas cards.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Janet H. Cho\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ***\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What to Watch on Jobs Friday\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists expect the U.S. economy to have added 477,500 jobs in March, as the labor market continued to tighten and employers competed for talent, bringing more workers in from the sidelines as the Covid-19 pandemic ebbs. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- The unemployment rate is expected to fall to 3.7%, down from 3.8% in \par       February, and would leave the jobless rate only slightly above its \par       prepandemic low of 3.5%, where it stood in February 2020. \par  \par    -- Hourly wages are expected to rise 0.4% in March from February, marking a \par       sizable increase from the sluggish 0.03% growth the month before. That \par       would put wage growth at a 5.5% annual pace, as employers hike pay to \par       lure in workers and more employees demand raises to keep up with rising \par       inflation. \par  \par    -- The jobs report will be closely monitored by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which \par       is expected to boost interest rates many times in 2022 and 2023 to curb \par       the steep increase in consumer prices. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What's Next: The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be keeping a close eye on the strength of the labor market as it prepares this monetary policy shift. A strong jobs report could strengthen the case for higher interest rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Joe Woelfel and Megan Cassella\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ***\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Metaverse Could Become a $13 Trillion Market by 2030\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The metaverse economy, encompassing virtual worlds such as gaming and virtual reality as well as smart manufacturing, online events, and digital \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , could become an $8 trillion to $13 trillion total market by 2030, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citi\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a research report. That would make it 1% of the $128 trillion global economy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Even though investments tied to the metaverse have been underperforming, \par       \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citi\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the metaverse could see five billion unique internet visitors \par       by the end of the decade, driving trillions of dollars in revenue. \par  \par    -- Metaverse gaming companies include Fortnite maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Epic Games\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Roblox\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \par       \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ubisoft Entertainment\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Microsoft\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which owns Minecraft. \par  \par    -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citi\f28 \uc2 \f2  is the latest banking giant to call the metaverse and web 3.0 a \par       multi-trillion-dollar opportunity. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  in December valued the \par       metaverse at $12.5 trillion, an outlook that assumes one-third of the \par       digital economy becomes virtual and then expands another 25%. \par  \par    -- Chip maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nvidia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's vision for the "omniverse," including industrial \par       applications and artificial-intelligence innovations, remains a key part \par       of analysts' optimism for its stock, which jumped 103% over the past \par       year. Shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Roblox\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a platform for building and experiencing virtual \par       worlds, have plummeted 31% over the past year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What's Next: MKM Partners analysts note \f28 \uc2 \f2 Roblox\f28 \uc2 \f2 's more-than-50 million daily active users, largely in the 5-to-24 age group. They think the platform's long-term total addressable market is one billion people, though their medium-term estimate is 180 million people.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Jack Denton and Janet H. Cho\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ***\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What to Watch on Streaming Platforms in April\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Streaming platforms \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple\f28 \uc2 \f2  TV, HBO Max, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Netflix\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hulu\f28 \uc2 \f2  are all launching new series and bringing back audience favorites for April ahead of the Emmys, \f28 \uc2 \f2 MarketWatch\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported. Five of the 10 films nominated for the best picture Oscar this year came from streaming services. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple\f28 \uc2 \f2 , whose CODA won the best picture Oscar, will show Slow Horses, a \par       British spy series adapted from Mick Herron's novels; Roar, a darkly \par       comic anthology series starring Nicole Kidman; and Pachinko, a \par       multigenerational miniseries based on Min Jin Lee's novel. \par  \par    -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 WarnerMedia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's HBO Max has Barry, starring Bill Hader as a hit man trying \par       to become an actor; The Flight Attendant, about an alcoholic in a murder \par       mystery; and Julia, a series about TV cook Julia Child. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Netflix\f28 \uc2 \f2  has \par       Russian Doll, a comedy about time-loopers, and the fourth season of dark \par       crime drama Ozark. \par  \par    -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hulu\f28 \uc2 \f2 , co-owned by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Walt Disney\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Comcast\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \uc2 \f2 NBCUniversal\f28 \uc2 \f2 , has The \par       Kardashians, a reality series that picks up where Keeping Up with the \par       Kardashians left off, and Under the Banner of Heaven, a drama miniseries \par       starring Andrew Garfield based on the Jon Krakauer book. \par  \par    -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Amazon.com\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Prime Video has supernatural Wyoming Western series Outer \par       Range, and A Very British Scandal, about the public divorce of the Duke \par       and Duchess of Argyll. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Disney\f28 \uc2 \f2  has Moon Knight, a darker, scarier and \par       stranger \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marvel\f28 \uc2 \f2  superhero series. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What's Next: \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Wrestling Entertainment\f28 \uc2 \f2  is now producing fictional TV shows, including Spanish-language comedy Contra las cuerdas ( Against the Ropes), about an aspiring female wrestler. Contra, which is currently in production, is slated to debut on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Netflix\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Mexico.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Janet H. Cho\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ***\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 These Tech Stocks Just Had Their Worst Quarter Ever\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors punished tech stocks during the first three months of 2022, resulting in the worst quarter in history for a dozen S&P 500 stocks. The S&P 500 fell 4.9% over the past three months, snapping a seven-quarter winning streak. The Nasdaq is down 9.1%. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Half the stocks that had their worst quarterly percentage declines as \par       tracked by Dow Jones Market Data Group are tech companies: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Etsy\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 PayPal\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \par       \f28 \uc2 \f2 Facebook\f28 \uc2 \f2  parent company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Meta Platforms\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Keysight Technologies\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Match \par       Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Charter Communications\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par  \par    -- The 12 stocks combined to lose $494.19 billion in market value. The bulk \par       of that came from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Facebook\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which dropped more than $300 billion in \par       valuation as investors chopped off roughly a third of its stock price, \par       \f28 \uc2 \f2 MarketWatch\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported. \par  \par    -- A change to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple\f28 \uc2 \f2 's mobile operating system slammed \f28 \uc2 \f2 Facebook\f28 \uc2 \f2  advertisers. \par       Other social-media stocks also took a hit for the quarter, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par       dropping 10%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Snap\f28 \uc2 \f2  falling more than 20% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pinterest\f28 \uc2 \f2  falling 30%. \par  \par    -- Other tech stocks had bad quarters but not record-setting ones. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Netflix\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par       fell 37.8%, its worst quarterly performance since the second quarter of \par       2012, while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Adobe\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell 19.7%, its worst since the third quarter of 2011. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1 Apr 2022 06:40 ET \par As Oil Briefly Dips Below $100, Russia and Europe -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What's Next: Charter benefited when people had to stay home during the pandemic, but now it's seeing a slowdown in broadband subscriber growth and is looking to the wireless business for its next big opportunity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Liz Moyer\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ***\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Do you remember this week's news? Take our quiz below about this week's news. Tell us how you did in an email to thebarronsdaily@barrons.com.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1. Which streaming service became the first to win best picture, for the feel-good movie CODA, at this year's Academy Awards?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a. Netflix b. Apple+ c. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hulu\f28 \uc2 \f2  d. Paramount+\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2. Which company indicated in a regulatory filing that it will seek to split its highly priced stock?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tesla\f28 \uc2 \f2  b. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Berkshire Hathaway\f28 \uc2 \f2  c. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chipotle Mexican Grill\f28 \uc2 \f2  d. \f28 \uc2 \f2 AutoZone\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3. What is included in Biden's proposed $5.8 trillion budget?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a. An increase in military spending b. An increase in funding for law enforcement c. A 20% minimum tax on the wealthiest Americans d. All of the above\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 4. Which insurer is spending about $5.4 billion to buy \f28 \uc2 \f2 LHC Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , one of the country's largest home-health companies?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a. \f28 \uc2 \f2 CVS Health\f28 \uc2 \f2  b. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Humana\f28 \uc2 \f2  c. \f28 \uc2 \f2 UnitedHealth Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  d. Anthem\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Mortgage Bankers Association\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported that credit availability rose to its highest level since last May. What steps are bankers taking to boost business?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a. Expanding product offerings b. Relaxing some borrower eligibility requirements c. A but not B d. A and B\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Answers: 1( b); 2( a); 3( d); 4( c); 5( d)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Barron's Staff\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ***\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Newsletter edited by Liz Moyer, Camilla Imperiali, Steve Goldstein, Rupert Steiner\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 01, 2022 06:40 ET (10:40 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020220401ei41001f2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
