\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Countries "hostile" to Russia will collect their debts with devalued rubles\b0\par\par\uc2 648 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW\par \par \uc2 The Russian government yesterday established a list of "hostile" countries, to which individuals and companies will be able to repay their debts in rubles, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that since the beginning of the invasion in Ukraine depreciated by more than 60 percent.\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin's measure, established through a presidential decree over the weekend, responds to the economic sanctions it received from the West in recent weeks due to the invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The list includes, among others, countries of the \uc2 European Union\uc2  (EU), Australia, USA, Canada, Switzerland and Japan.\par \par \uc2 As of this measure, Russian companies will be able to pay creditors in these countries in rubles, even if the securities are denominated in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For this purpose, the debtor will be able to ask a Russian bank to create a special ruble account in the name of the foreign creditor and send him a payment in Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the amount due, at the exchange rate of the day in question, as indicated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of that country.\par \par \uc2 This measure shall apply to payments in excess of 10 million rubles per month.\par \par \uc2 SPECIAL PERMISSION TO OTHER COUNTRIES\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, countries that are not part of the lists will still be able to receive payments in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  through a special permit.\par \par \uc2 This is one of Russia's first responses to sanctions imposed by numerous foreign countries following its military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to show that it can still meet its financial obligations, in a context of uncertainty in which it is believed that it may default.\par \par \uc2 To counter the fall of the ruble, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's government established various measures, including prohibiting its residents from transferring foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  abroad; charging a 30 percent commission to exchange rubles into dollars, euros or pounds; and obliging exporters to convert 80 percent of their revenues earned in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  into rubles.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls cast a pall of doubt over whether or not Russia can pay its foreign creditors.\par \par \uc2 Although last Wednesday Russia paid $98 million of a sovereign debt coupon (OFZ) in rubles, foreign holders did not receive the money due to restrictions on foreign payments, generating a debate on whether or not it has already defaulted.\par \par \uc2 On March 16 there will be another round of maturities for 117 million dollars that do not allow payment in another \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If Russia decides to pay in rubles, the country could eventually default and trigger credit default swaps (CDS), the insurance for creditors in case of default, whose values rebounded yesterday to a figure that indicates that the country has an 80 percent chance of defaulting.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, \uc2 Moody's\uc2  downgraded for the second time in less than seven days its long-term local and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt rating from B3 to Ca, only one notch above the default rating.\par \par \uc2 The rating agency explained that the downgrade was triggered by the expectation that capital controls introduced by \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will restrict cross-border payments, including on government bond debt service.\par \par \uc2 "The downgrade to 'Ca' is driven by serious concerns about Russia's willingness and ability to service its debt obligations," \uc2 Moody's\uc2  justified, for which the risk of a default occurring "has increased significantly."\par \par \uc2 The provision comes on top of a similar downgrade by the \uc2 Fitch\uc2  agency last week, and the reclassification of the MSCI Russia index from "Emerging Market" to "Isolated Market".\par \par \uc2 CLOSED STOCK MARKET\par \par \uc2 In this context, the Russian stock exchange has been closed since February 25, the day after the start of the Russian offensive in Ukraine. Since that date, the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost almost half of its value. (AFP and AP)\par \par \uc2 The "hostile" list includes countries of the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , the USA, Australia and Canada, among others.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220308ei38003zy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
