\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia issued a list of the countries it considers hostile\b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Russian government issued a list of all countries it considers hostile: all countries of the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , the United States, Japan and Canada, as well as foreign territories that, according to Moscow, commit hostile actions against the Russian Federation, Russian companies and citizens.\par \par \uc2 Follow live the conflict between Russia and UkraineAccording to the Russian news agency Interfax, the order with the listing has been signed by the Prime Minister, \uc2 Mikhail Mishustin\uc2 , and is part of the Decree of the President of the Russian Federation issued on March 5, 2022 "On the temporary procedure for fulfilling obligations to certain foreign creditors".\par \par \uc2 In addition to the countries already mentioned, the list also includes Australia, Albania, Andorra, United Kingdom, Iceland, Liechtenstein, Micronesia, Monaco, New Zealand, Norway, Republic of Korea, San Marino, North Macedonia, Singapore, Taiwan, Montenegro, Switzerland and Ukraine itself.\par \par \uc2 What about countries declared "hostile" by Russia?According to the Kremlin, individuals and companies will be able to repay their debts in rubles - a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has lost 45% of its value since January - to countries declared hostile.\par \par \uc2 The debtor will be able to ask a Russian bank to create a special ruble account in the name of the foreign creditor and send him a payment in Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the amount due, at the exchange rate of the day in question, as indicated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This measure will apply to payments exceeding 10 million rubles per month.\par \par \uc2 This is one of the first Russian responses to the unprecedented sanctions imposed on \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  by numerous foreign countries following its military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220307ei37007ou\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
