\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia adopts list of "hostile" countries to be reimbursed in rubles\b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Russian authorities established a list of countries "hostile" to the country, to which individuals and companies will be able to repay their debts in rubles, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has lost 45% of its value since January, the government said Monday.\par \par \uc2 This list of countries, prepared following a presidential decree on Friday that refers to a "provisional procedure," includes, among others, \uc2 European Union\uc2  (EU) countries, Australia, the United States, Canada, the United States, Switzerland and Japan.\par \par \uc2 To this end, the debtor will be able to ask a Russian bank to create a special ruble account in the name of the foreign creditor and send him a payment in Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the amount due, at the exchange rate of the day in question, as indicated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This measure will apply to payments exceeding 10 million rubles per month.\par \par \uc2 This is one of the first Russian responses to the unprecedented sanctions imposed on \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  by numerous foreign countries following its military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The sanctions caused the historic depreciation of the ruble and are accompanied by the freezing of part of the authorities' funds abroad, which prevents the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from supporting the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was exchanging this Monday morning at 137.70 rubles to the dollar. Since January 1 it has lost 45% of its value.\par \par \uc2 Hostile countries\par \par \uc2 The list, in addition to states, also includes foreign territories that, according to Moscow, commit hostile actions against the Russian Federation, Russian companies and citizens.\par \par \uc2 According to Interfax, the order with the list has been signed by Prime Minister \uc2 Mikhail Mishustin\uc2  and is part of the Decree of the President of the Russian Federation issued on March 5, 2022 "On the temporary procedure for fulfilling obligations to certain foreign creditors".\par \par \uc2 According to this document, the list includes the 27 member states of the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , who have approved strong sanctions against Russia after its invasion of Ukraine last February 24.\par \par \uc2 But other countries such as Australia, Albania, Andorra, Great Britain (including the island of Jersey and other overseas territories it controls: such as the island of Anguilla, the British Virgin Islands and Gibraltar), Iceland and Liechtenstein are also defined as hostile countries.\par \par \uc2 Also in the relationship are Micronesia, Monaco, New Zealand, Norway, Republic of Korea, San Marino, North Macedonia, Singapore, Taiwan, Montenegro, Switzerland, Japan and Ukraine itself.\par \par \uc2 Source: AFP and EFE\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220307ei37006dc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
