\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Ruble plunges more than 20% in week because of sanctions on Russia\b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The ruble ended the week down more than 20% against the dollar and euro in Moscow trading on Friday (4), with the Russian economy under pressure from sanctions aimed at isolating Russia in response to its invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The ruble ended the week at 115 per dollar in Moscow, down from 83 per dollar last Friday, though it appreciated 1% on Friday over Thursday. Against the euro it closed just below 119 per euro, down from 93 per euro at the end of last week. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit record lows against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday and the euro on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has plummeted more than 20 percent this week - Dado Ruvic/Reuters "Russian assets are being destroyed in value," said \uc2 Cristian Maggio\uc2 , head of portfolio strategy at \uc2 TD Securities\par \par \uc2 . Russia's five-year CDS -- a measure of the cost of protection against a debt default -- stood at 1,565 basis points, up from Thursday's 1,412 basis points, but still some distance from Monday's record 1,973 basis points, data from \uc2 IHS Markit\uc2  showed.\par \par \uc2 Trading on the Moscow Stock Exchange remained virtually closed on Friday, the fifth day of restrictions imposed by the \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In spot market trading outside Russia, the ruble was down 10.4 percent at 121.033 per dollar in mid-afternoon New York after hitting a record low of 122.033 per dollar. Buying and selling offers were between 120 and 128 per dollar, which traders characterized as a sign of evaporating liquidity.\par \par \uc2 For the week, the ruble was down 30.7%, deepening the 2022 low to 36.2%.\par \par \uc2 G7\uc2  threatens Russia with new sanctions The group of seven most industrialized countries in the world (\uc2 G7\uc2 ) threatened on Friday (4) to impose new "severe sanctions" against \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  for its military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine and proposed to counter Russian "disinformation" campaigns about the war.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 G7\uc2  countries "will continue to impose severe sanctions in response to Russian aggression," the foreign ministers of the group formed by the United States, Canada, France, the United Kingdom, Germany, Italy and Japan said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 G7\uc2  also indicated that it will act to curb the "Russian disinformation campaign," which "puts more lives at risk."\par \par \uc2 The statement urged Russia to end its attacks "in the vicinity of Ukrainian nuclear power plants," following Russian bombings that on Friday caused a fire at the Zaporizhzhia plant, Europe's largest, with no consequences on radioactivity levels.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220304ei34009n0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
