85B0721100016F800C0FA003C0A0003AC00D76700D70800057F005C0C004D81180035AE0015A900A77500C86E12C301110003B}}
\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 From Russian state to Croatian and Slovenian states: the end for  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2 's largest bank in the \uc2 European Union\b0\par\par\uc2 1,100 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  over \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's largest bank, \uc2 Sberbank\uc2 , has dictated its expulsion from the \uc2 European Union\uc2 . The heart of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in Austria, is going into insolvency, and the subsidiaries in Croatia and Slovenia have new owners: among them are the Croatian and Slovenian states themselves. This is, therefore, a change of ownership states. After the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Russian bank itself came to say that it was leaving the continent (with the exception of Switzerland).\par \par \uc2 It had been known since Monday that, after the deposit flight, the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had given the go-ahead for everything to be different in the European arms of \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  by giving it the stamp of "at risk or insolvent". With this, preparations began on the part of the \uc2 Single Resolution Board\uc2 , which is responsible in Europe for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in European banks.\par \par \uc2 The Russian bank in the euro zone carries the same label as Banif and Popular: "at risk or insolvent. What is at stake?\par \par \uc2 The decision, after a two-day moratorium, was taken on March 1st, and came with different positions: on one side, Austrian insolvency; on the other, Croatian and Slovenian continuity. In the case of deposits, there is a protection of up to 100 thousand euros in the applications made in the Austrian bank, and a total guarantee on the applications placed in the Croatian and Slovenian banks, as they pass to another owner.\par \par \uc2 No money from the Single Resolution Fund "Today, we acted to protect the public interest and ensure financial stability. All this was done without having to use public funds, so not only were \uc2 Sberbank\uc2 's customers protected, but taxpayers were too," said Single Council President \uc2 Elke K\u246\'00\'F6nig\uc2 . The \uc2 European Commission\uc2  supported the \uc2 Single Resolution Board\uc2 's decision, the implementation of which is now up to each of the national authorities.\par \par \uc2 There is no aid from the Single Resolution Fund, to which European banks contribute to pay for difficulties in a banking entity, as the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  points out in the decision authorizing the resolution measure. This means that Portuguese banks are not contributing to these \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The banks were at risk of insolvency, there were no private solutions outside the resolution regime, there were no supervisory actions to prevent insolvency, and the resolution action was necessary in the public interest," according to the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Even if there is no European money directly, the truth is that the new owners have taxpayer money involved.\par \par \uc2 The new state owners "The \uc2 Single Resolution Board\uc2  has decided to transfer all shares in \uc2 Sberbank\uc2 's subsidiary in Croatia to \uc2 Hrvatska Po\u353\'01\'61tanska Banka d.d\uc2 Hrvatska Po\u353\'01\'61tanska Banka\uc2  d.d. [HPB, the Croatian postal bank] and all shares in Sbrebank's subsidiary in Slovenia to Nova ljubljanska banka (NLB)." This option means that the banks opened this Wednesday, March 2, without any problems for either depositors or customers. "They are now part of well-established, robust and stable banking groups."\par \par \uc2 In the case of the Croatian business, the new shareholder of the Russian bank, HPB, is a Croatian state-owned institution with a market share of 5.6% of the assets of the Balkan country's banking system. The Croatian Republic holds 45% of the capital, followed by other Croatian entities, such as the postal service company and the deposit guarantee and pension system.\par \par \uc2 The Croatian authorities point out "that all deposits by citizens and companies, regardless of volume, are absolutely safe. In the Slovenian case, too.\par \par \uc2 The Slovenian institution that takes over the country's \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  is owned by the Republic of Slovenia. \uc2 NBL\uc2  is the largest international bank in the country, and it is public - it was recently privatized, with the Slovenian state holding 25% of the capital, which is the largest shareholder. It has other shareholders, including \uc2 Schroders\uc2  and the \uc2 EBRD\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Austrian and Czech insolvency In the opposite direction goes the bank in Austria: "The \uc2 Single Resolution Board\uc2  has decided that resolution of the Austrian Sberbabank Europe AG is not necessary. Insolvency proceedings will be followed according to national law," indicates its communiqu\u233\'00\'E9.\par \par \uc2 The authority's conclusion is that this unit, although it was the heart of the other entities, did not perform "critical functions" for the economy, and that insolvency would not have a negative impact on Austrian financial stability ("its discontinuation would not cause disruption to services that are essential for Austria's real economy, nor disruption to financial stability in Austria and other member states").\par \par \uc2 According to the Austrian supervisor, who follows the instructions of the \uc2 ECB\uc2  (which is the institution's direct supervisory authority), the deposit guarantee scheme will have to pay up to 100,000 euros per application within 10 working days.\par \par \uc2 If the Austrian bank ceases to exist, the free provision of services it had in Portugal will also cease to exist.\par \par \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  and \uc2 VTB\uc2 : the banks most affected by the sanctions have ramifications as far as Angola and Vietnam (and a discreet connection to Portugal)\par \par \uc2 Sidelined by others and on its own \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  has a presence in other European countries, but these three entities were those that, being autonomous, were under the direct supervision of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to the cross-border dimension of the group. In the Czech Republic, the \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  unit - which was not directly supervised by the \uc2 ECB\uc2 , but by the national authority - has already had its banking license revoked and is also ensuring the payment of deposits of up to 100,000 euros in the next seven days. The Czech guarantee scheme has already ensured that it has the money to pay out all eligible deposits.\par \par \uc2 This is the step that dictates the future of \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  in Europe which even had an agreement since last year to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Bosnia and Herzegovina, Croatia, Hungary, Serbia and Slovenia - the Russian war ended those plans. The end happened and without receiving any money.\par \par \uc2 Moscow Stock Exchange closed, largest Russian bank abandons European market\par \par \uc2 By the way, in addition to the decision of the European banking authorities, \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  also announced the withdrawal of its presence from Europe (with the exception of Switzerland). According to a statement quoted by the international press, the \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ordered the exit from Europe due to inability to provide liquidity to European subsidiaries - foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to be kept in the country. In addition to the decision, the Russian group also justifies the exit with the "threats to the safety of employees and branches" felt in the countries, as quoted by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220302ei32007r8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
