\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Today's world news highlights Tuesday, March 1\b0\par\par\uc2 1,505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Iran's Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei attributed the situation around Ukraine to U.S. policy and actions.\par \par \uc2 - Russia will continue the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine until it achieves its goals according to Defense Ministry\par \par \uc2 Moscow, 1 Mar ???.- Russian Defense Minister \uc2 Sergey Shoigu\uc2  said Tuesday that the military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched in Ukraine will continue until Moscow achieves its objectives.\par \par \uc2 - Kremlin dismisses as a hoax reports on use of cluster bombs by Russian forces in Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Moscow, Mar 1 .- Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said that reports about the alleged use of cluster and thermobaric bombs by Russian forces in Ukraine do not correspond to reality.\par \par \uc2 - Kremlin considers it premature to assess the results of negotiations with Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Moscow, March 1 - It is still premature to assess the results of the negotiations that Russia and Ukraine held on Monday, Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said.\par \par \uc2 - Russia sees unwillingness of Ukraine to find legitimate and balanced solution to the crisis\par \par \uc2 Moscow, March 2 - Moscow sees no willingness on the part of Kiev to seek a legitimate and balanced solution to the crisis, said Russia's permanent representative to the \uc2 UN\uc2  headquarters in Geneva, Guennadi Gatilov.\par \par \uc2 - Venezuelan Vice-President accuses \uc2 UN Human Rights Council\uc2  of promoting hatred against Russia\par \par \uc2 Caracas, Mar. 2 - Venezuelan Vice President \uc2 Delcy Rodriguez\uc2  on Tuesday accused the United Nations (\uc2 UN\uc2 ) Human Rights Council of promoting hatred and intolerance against Russia, and pointed out that member countries are responsible for the current crisis in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 - ICJ to consider Ukraine's claim against Russia on 7-8 March\par \par \uc2 Paris, Mar 1 .- The \uc2 International Court of Justice\uc2  in The Hague (ICJ) will hold hearings on March 7 and 8 on Ukraine's lawsuit with accusations against Russia of genocide.\par \par \uc2 - Putin bans transfer abroad of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an amount greater than $10,000\par \par \uc2 Moscow, Mar 1 - Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  on Tuesday signed a decree banning the transfer of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  abroad in an amount exceeding $10,000, the Kremlin said.\par \par \uc2 - Zelenski reiterates readiness for negotiations with Putin\par \par \uc2 Moscow, March 1 - \uc2 Vladimir Zelensky\uc2  declared that he is ready for peace negotiations with Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 International Energy Agency\uc2  Ministers Discuss Reducing Dependence on Russian Gas\par \par \uc2 Washington, Mar. 1 - Europe needs to reduce its dependence on Russian natural gas and seek alternative energy sources including renewables, \uc2 International Energy Agency\uc2  (\uc2 IEA\uc2 ) ministers said Tuesday after announcing an emergency release of crude oil stocks due to supply concerns amid the crisis between Russia and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 - Zelenski demands cessation of hostilities in Ukraine for negotiations with Russia\par \par \uc2 Moscow, Mar. 1 - \uc2 Vladimir Zelensky\uc2  insisted on the need to cease hostilities in Ukraine before holding negotiations between Kiev and Moscow on the Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 - Maduro expresses strong support for Russia's decisive actions in Ukraine to Putin\par \par \uc2 Moscow, Mar. 1 - Venezuelan President Nicolas Maduro in a telephone conversation with Russian leader \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  expressed his strong support for Russia's military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine, the Kremlin press service reported.\par \par \uc2 - U.S. has no indication of Belarusian troops entering Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Washington, Mar 1 .- The U.S. administration sees no signs that Belarusian troops are entering Ukraine, a senior Pentagon official said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 - Projectile hits communications tower in Kiev, media say\par \par \uc2 Moscow, Mar 1 .- Ukrainian media publish images of an explosion at a communications tower in Kiev, claiming it was hit by a projectile.\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE REFUGEES\par \par \uc2 - At least 660,000 refugees flee Ukraine since February 24 according to \uc2 UNHCR\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Geneva (Switzerland), Mar 1 .- The total number of refugees who have fled Ukraine since the start of Russia's military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to 660,000, \uc2 UN High Commissioner for Refugees\uc2  (\uc2 UNHCR\uc2 ) spokeswoman Shabia Mantoo said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA SANCTIONS\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Disney\uc2  suspends release of its films in Russia over Ukraine crisis\par \par \uc2 Moscow, Mar 1 .- \uc2 The Walt Disney Company\uc2  announced Monday that it is suspending the release of its films in Russia in response to the crisis in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 - Mastercard blocks "multiple institutions" in compliance with sanctions on Russia\par \par \uc2 Moscow, Mar. 1 - Multinational financial services company \uc2 Mastercard\uc2  announced Monday it has blocked "multiple institutions" in compliance with sanctions imposed on \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  for its military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 - UK includes financial institution \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  in its list of Russian sanctioned institutions\par \par \uc2 London, Mar. 1 - \uc2 Sberbank\uc2 , Russia's largest financial institution in state assets, has been added to the official list of sanctioned financial institutions in the United Kingdom, according to the latest update issued by the Treasury.\par \par \uc2 - Austrian regulator suspends \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  subsidiary's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Vienna, Mar. 2 - The \uc2 Austrian Financial Markets Authority\uc2  announced that, following instructions from the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 ECB\uc2 ), it banned \uc2 Sberbank Europe AG\uc2 , a subsidiary of the largest Russian bank \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  based in Austria, from continuing its business \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 - Canada prepares new sanctions against Russia\par \par \uc2 Toronto (Canada), Mar 2 .- Canada and its allies are preparing new sanctions against Russia in response to its special military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine, the North American country's Finance Minister \uc2 Chrystia Freeland\uc2  said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 - Canada is reviewing the involvement of all Russian "oligarchs" and companies in the country.\par \par \uc2 Toronto, Mar. 2 - Canada is reviewing the holdings of all so-called Russian oligarchs and companies in the country, Finance Minister \uc2 Chrystia Freeland\uc2  said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Apple\uc2  announces it paused product sales in Russia and limited other services\par \par \uc2 Washington, Mar 1 .- U.S. technology and online services company \uc2 Apple\uc2  announced Tuesday a pause in product sales in Russia and limited the \uc2 Apple\uc2  Pay mobile payment service, among others, in response to Russia's special military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 - Turkey does not plan to impose sanctions on Russia\par \par \uc2 Ankara, Mar 1 .- Turkey does not plan to impose sanctions on Russia over its military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine, Turkish President's spokesman \uc2 Ibrahim Kalin\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 - UK sanctions \uc2 Russian Direct Investment Fund\uc2 , Sputnik V vaccine investor\par \par \uc2 London, Mar. 1 - The United Kingdom imposed sanctions against the \uc2 Russian Direct Investment Fund\uc2  (\uc2 RDIF\uc2 ) - investor in the Sputnik V coronavirus vaccine - and its chief executive, Kiril Dmitriev, over the Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine, according to the list of sanctioned parties published on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 - Canada bans Russian fishing vessels from entering ports and inland waters\par \par \uc2 Washington, Mar. 1 - The \uc2 Government of Canada\uc2  on Tuesday banned Russian ships and fishing vessels from entering its ports and inland waters.\par \par \uc2 - Mexico rules out economic retaliation against Russia and condemns censorship\par \par \uc2 Mexico City, Mar 1 - Mexican President \uc2 Andres Manuel Lopez Obrador\uc2  said Tuesday that the Latin American country will not take economic reprisals against Russia and condemned censorship in the media following a military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Moscow in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 SPUTNIK GOOGLE TWITTER\par \par \uc2 - Sputnik agency denounces labeling of its employees' \uc2 Twitter\uc2  accounts\par \par \uc2 Moscow, March 1 - The Sputnik news agency denounced the labeling of its employees' \uc2 Twitter\uc2  accounts by the social network itself, which it called a witch hunt.\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Google\uc2  blocks access to RT and Sputnik \uc2 YouTube\uc2  channels in Europe\par \par \uc2 Moscow, Mar 1 .- \uc2 YouTube\uc2  channels linked to Russian media RT and Sputnik will be blocked in Europe because of the military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine, \uc2 Google\uc2  reported Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 BRENT OIL PRICE\par \par \uc2 - Global benchmark Brent oil index settles at August 2014 figures.\par \par \uc2 New York, Mar 1 .- Global oil prices, as measured by the Brent crude benchmark index, settled at 7.5-year highs on Tuesday as the crisis between Russia and Ukraine intensified and oil traders feared that Western sanctions against Moscow would severely affect the country's energy exports.\par \par \uc2 ARGENTINA MALVINAS\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2  asks to continue with the identification of soldiers fallen in Malvinas\par \par \uc2 Buenos Aires, Mar. 1 - \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2  announced that he asked the \uc2 International Committee of the Red Cross\uc2  (\uc2 ICRC\uc2 ) to launch a third phase of the Humanitarian Project Plan supervised by the organization to identify combatants buried in the Darwin cemetery of the Malvinas Islands.\par \par \uc2 OIL RESERVES\par \par \uc2 - Oil-consuming countries release 60 million barrels from emergency reserves\par \par \uc2 Washington, March 1 - Oil consuming countries will release 60 million barrels of crude oil from their emergency reserves in a coordinated action aimed at avoiding shortages caused by the crisis between Russia and Ukraine, the \uc2 International Energy Agency\uc2  (\uc2 IEA\uc2 ) announced Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 ARGENTINA CHINA SWAP\par \par \uc2 - Argentina to extend its swap agreement with China, President announces\par \par \uc2 Buenos Aires, Mar 1 - Argentina's President \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2  announced that he has reached an agreement with the Chinese government of \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  to extend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap available to the country and thus increase its reserves.\par \par \uc2 ARGENTINA IMF PAYMENTS\par \par \uc2 - Argentina will start payments to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  in 2026 and will finish in 2034, says president\par \par \uc2 Buenos Aires, Mar 1 - Argentina's President \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2  announced on Tuesday that he reached an agreement with the staff of the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) whereby the country will refinance its $44 billion debt with a payment schedule that will begin in 2026 and end in 2034.\par \par \uc2 ARGENTINA ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 - Argentina's economy recovered 10.3% in 2021, says president\par \par \uc2 Buenos Aires, Mar 1 .- In 2021, Argentina's Gross Domestic Product (GDP) improved 10.3 percent, President \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2  highlighted Tuesday while addressing deputies and senators during the opening of the 140th ordinary session of Congress.\par \par \uc2 Source: Sputnik\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220301ei3100679\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
